{"jobs":[{"id":"d1c99cf9-eb9b-444c-bf5b-9b0f776e78a5","title":"Senior Accountant","department":"Business","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T21:17:53.833+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d1c99cf9-eb9b-444c-bf5b-9b0f776e78a5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d1c99cf9-eb9b-444c-bf5b-9b0f776e78a5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Accountant, you will play an important role in supporting Grow Therapy's accounting operations and financial close process. Reporting to the Head of Accounting, this role will own key close processes, support external audit and tax compliance, and partner cross-functionally to strengthen financial controls and build scalable processes. This role offers the opportunity to own and scale core accounting workstreams, including revenue/accounts receivable, cost of sales/provider payouts, intercompany, and treasury.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own core accounting processes across Revenue and Accounts Receivable, Cost of Services and Provider Payouts, Intercompany, and Treasury, ensuring accuracy, timeliness, and compliance with US GAAP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own key balance sheet accounts and drive the month-end close through the preparation of journal entries, accruals, account reconciliations, and monthly fluctuation analyses, ensuring the accuracy and completeness of financial results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assess new partnerships and revenue streams, applying ASC 606 revenue recognition principles to evaluate contracts, document technical accounting conclusions, and ensure new arrangements are recorded appropriately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support external financial audits and income tax compliance by preparing workpapers, gathering documentation, and serving as a key point of contact for auditors and tax advisors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and implement AI-driven efficiencies across accounting workflows, partnering cross-functionally to reduce manual effort, strengthen controls, and ensure processes scale with the business.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of accounting experience with a mix of public accounting and industry, and an active CPA preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field with a solid working knowledge of US GAAP, including experience researching and applying technical accounting concepts (revenue recognition/ASC 606 a plus).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with ERP systems (NetSuite preferred) and advanced proficiency in Excel; experience with Power Query is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment while managing multiple priorities and deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A continuous improvement mindset paired with curiosity about AI tools: you document what you build, think in systems, and leave processes better than you found them.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> $114,000 - $133,000 USD Annually</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will be <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>)<strong>.</strong> The  hybrid arrangement will include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\n\nAs a Senior Accountant, you will play an important role in supporting Grow Therapy's accounting operations and financial close process. Reporting to the Head of Accounting, this role will own key close processes, support external audit and tax compliance, and partner cross-functionally to strengthen financial controls and build scalable processes. This role offers the opportunity to own and scale core accounting workstreams, including revenue/accounts receivable, cost of sales/provider payouts, intercompany, and treasury.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Own core accounting processes across Revenue and Accounts Receivable, Cost of Services and Provider Payouts, Intercompany, and Treasury, ensuring accuracy, timeliness, and compliance with US GAAP.\n\n - Own key balance sheet accounts and drive the month-end close through the preparation of journal entries, accruals, account reconciliations, and monthly fluctuation analyses, ensuring the accuracy and completeness of financial results.\n\n - Assess new partnerships and revenue streams, applying ASC 606 revenue recognition principles to evaluate contracts, document technical accounting conclusions, and ensure new arrangements are recorded appropriately.\n\n - Support external financial audits and income tax compliance by preparing workpapers, gathering documentation, and serving as a key point of contact for auditors and tax advisors.\n\n - Architect and implement AI-driven efficiencies across accounting workflows, partnering cross-functionally to reduce manual effort, strengthen controls, and ensure processes scale with the business.\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - 5+ years of accounting experience with a mix of public accounting and industry, and an active CPA preferred.\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field with a solid working knowledge of US GAAP, including experience researching and applying technical accounting concepts (revenue recognition/ASC 606 a plus).\n\n - Experience with ERP systems (NetSuite preferred) and advanced proficiency in Excel; experience with Power Query is a plus.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment while managing multiple priorities and deadlines.\n\n - A continuous improvement mindset paired with curiosity about AI tools: you document what you build, think in systems, and leave processes better than you found them.\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\nHybrid Commitment: $114,000 - $133,000 USD Annually\n\nThis role will be hybrid (onsite from our NYC location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday). The  hybrid arrangement will include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$114K – $133K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$114K - $133K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3f4a5ce4-f086-4435-92b6-74e25d7416bd","tierSummary":"$114K – $133K","title":"Hub","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"90495cb4-200e-4232-8778-a6fca412f07c","summary":"$114K – $133K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":114000,"maxValue":133000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":114000,"maxValue":133000}]}},{"id":"b2ff7626-cd25-4f2a-851c-6b77345209a5","title":"Senior/Staff Product Designer, Growth","department":"Technology","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2025-07-08T13:33:23.784+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/b2ff7626-cd25-4f2a-851c-6b77345209a5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/b2ff7626-cd25-4f2a-851c-6b77345209a5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><br />The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Senior or Staff Product Designer to join our Product Growth team. This role will shape how clients discover and navigate early parts of their experience with Grow Therapy. The Product Growth team is within our Match Success org, one of Grow's highest-priority areas where we help clients identify their needs, evaluate potential providers, and get them started on their therapy journey. You'll lead 0→1 design work — from strategy through launch — impacting millions of people looking for mental health support, and set the craft bar for how growth-focused design gets done at Grow.<br /><br /><strong>What You'll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore a wide array of hypotheses and problems and then strive to create a clear point of view on what to build, translating business goals and client needs into concrete design briefs and roadmap milestones</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring clarity to ambiguous, cross-team growth problems — funnel drop-off, activation friction, new programs, channel optimizations — and turn them into shippable design work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and prototype end-to-end, from early concept through high-fidelity design and production handoff, staying close through iteration to resolve issues as they arise</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion design excellence by treating product as an extension of of our brand, ensuring every touchpoint meets the highest quality standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product Management, Data Science, and Engineering to design and interpret experiments, using quantitative and qualitative signals to inform design decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI-powered tools as a natural part of your workflow to prototype faster, explore more directions, and multiply your own and your team's output without sacrificing craft</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of end-to-end (UX and UI) product design experience on consumer-facing or marketplace products; growth team experience a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Portfolio demonstrating craft excellence, systems thinking, and leadership through influence—shipped outcomes, not just polished mocks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong visual design sensibility, with range across systemized UI and more expressive, brand-forward work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading design on high-impact projects, including giving direction and feedback to other designers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think strategically about product vision — not just how something should look, but what should be built and why</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience shipping applications or software across mobile and web</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skilled at using AI as a creative and productivity multiplier, moving faster and exploring more ideas without sacrificing judgment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills, able to articulate and defend design decisions to both design and non-design partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience establishing design workflows, systems, and team practices that scale beyond a single project</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to collaborate effectively with Engineering, PM, and other disciplines as true partners, not just stakeholders</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment Type: Full Time</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC or SF hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (ex. team workshops, hackathons, company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.<br /><br /><strong>Role Details:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type: </strong>Full Time, Exempt<strong><br />Base Compensation: </strong>The base compensation range for this position is:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> $182,000 - 227,000 USD Annually</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is hybrid (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday). Expect to travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nWe're looking for a Senior or Staff Product Designer to join our Product Growth team. This role will shape how clients discover and navigate early parts of their experience with Grow Therapy. The Product Growth team is within our Match Success org, one of Grow's highest-priority areas where we help clients identify their needs, evaluate potential providers, and get them started on their therapy journey. You'll lead 0→1 design work — from strategy through launch — impacting millions of people looking for mental health support, and set the craft bar for how growth-focused design gets done at Grow.\n\nWhat You'll Be Doing:\n\n - Explore a wide array of hypotheses and problems and then strive to create a clear point of view on what to build, translating business goals and client needs into concrete design briefs and roadmap milestones\n\n - Bring clarity to ambiguous, cross-team growth problems — funnel drop-off, activation friction, new programs, channel optimizations — and turn them into shippable design work\n\n - Design and prototype end-to-end, from early concept through high-fidelity design and production handoff, staying close through iteration to resolve issues as they arise\n\n - Champion design excellence by treating product as an extension of of our brand, ensuring every touchpoint meets the highest quality standards\n\n - Partner with Product Management, Data Science, and Engineering to design and interpret experiments, using quantitative and qualitative signals to inform design decisions\n\n - Use AI-powered tools as a natural part of your workflow to prototype faster, explore more directions, and multiply your own and your team's output without sacrificing craft\n\nYou'll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - 6+ years of end-to-end (UX and UI) product design experience on consumer-facing or marketplace products; growth team experience a plus\n\n - Portfolio demonstrating craft excellence, systems thinking, and leadership through influence—shipped outcomes, not just polished mocks\n\n - Strong visual design sensibility, with range across systemized UI and more expressive, brand-forward work\n\n - Experience leading design on high-impact projects, including giving direction and feedback to other designers\n\n - Ability to think strategically about product vision — not just how something should look, but what should be built and why\n\n - Experience shipping applications or software across mobile and web\n\n - Skilled at using AI as a creative and productivity multiplier, moving faster and exploring more ideas without sacrificing judgment\n\n - Excellent communication skills, able to articulate and defend design decisions to both design and non-design partners\n\n - Experience establishing design workflows, systems, and team practices that scale beyond a single project\n\n - Proven ability to collaborate effectively with Engineering, PM, and other disciplines as true partners, not just stakeholders\n\n\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC or SF hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (ex. team workshops, hackathons, company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.\n\nRole Details:\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\n - Hybrid Commitment: $182,000 - 227,000 USD Annually\n\nThis role is hybrid (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday). Expect to travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$182K – $227K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$182K - $227K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f47a9229-6d84-49f6-8b11-5ac610e065ff","tierSummary":"$182K – $227K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"84570e61-1ebb-4083-b3c5-31e34b47453a","summary":"$182K – $227K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":227000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":227000}]}},{"id":"16179a07-5099-4034-941c-7b2f28d91e83","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Backend","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-03-30T19:16:53.312+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/16179a07-5099-4034-941c-7b2f28d91e83","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/16179a07-5099-4034-941c-7b2f28d91e83/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring a Software Engineer to help build and evolve the backend systems that power Grow Therapy's platform. In this role, you'll design, implement, and ship server-side features and services that directly impact how clients and providers connect, communicate, and access care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll join a collaborative, product-focused engineering organization where technical work is closely tied to reliability, scalability, and real-world outcomes. This role is ideal for an engineer who takes pride in writing clean, well-tested code, thinks carefully about system design and data integrity, and is energized by the opportunity to grow alongside a fast-moving team.</p><h2><strong>Why This Role Matters</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Access to mental healthcare in America is still deeply fragmented and Grow Therapy is building the platform to fix that. We connect clients, providers, and health plans in a single integrated system, and the software our engineers ship directly shapes whether people can find and afford the care they need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're growing fast - nearly 22,000 clinicians, over 1.4 million clients, and on track to surpass 10 million sessions in 2026 and we see ourselves as a generational company with a long way still to go. Engineers who join now have a real opportunity to build systems that matter at meaningful scale.</p><h2><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own backend services and APIs end to end — from technical design through implementation, deployment, and ongoing reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive architectural decisions within your team, bringing structure and clarity to complex, ambiguous problem spaces</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead improvements to core platform systems, including data pipelines, service reliability, and business logic</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and enable safe, repeatable experimentation through robust A/B testing and analysis workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Diagnose and resolve data quality, performance, and correctness issues across systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, well-tested, maintainable production code and set a high bar through code reviews and technical mentorship</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product, Design, and Data to translate goals into technical designs and execution plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape the technical direction of your team and contribute meaningfully to cross-team architectural discussions</p></li></ul><h2><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If You Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of professional software engineering experience with meaningful ownership of production backend systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep backend engineering expertise, including service design, data modeling, and API development at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and operating systems where reliability, data quality, and performance are critical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to operate in ambiguous problem spaces and drive clarity across technical and cross-functional stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A highly data-driven mindset, comfortable with experimentation, measurement, and optimization from both product and technical perspectives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A product-minded approach — you understand how technical decisions impact user experience and business outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong collaboration and communication skills, with a track record of influencing cross-functional partners including Product, Design, and Data Science</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using AI-assisted dev tools (e.g., Cursor, GitHub Copilot)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward ownership, speed, learning, and continuous improvement</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Engineering Team Overviews</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Marketplace Experience<br /></strong>The Marketplace Experience team shapes how clients discover and evaluate providers on Grow, transforming a simple directory into a guided, personalized entry point to care. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll work across search, ranking, profiles, and booking flows to build a fast, resilient, and intelligent marketplace that helps every client find the right fit provider and convert that intent into a booked appointment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Client Activation<br /></strong>The Client Activation team owns the fragile moments between booking and a client’s first few sessions, making starting care feel clear, reliable, and supportive. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build and harden systems for scheduling, authentication, notifications, and early-journey flows that directly determine whether clients show up, come back for visit two, and build lasting relationships with their providers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Claims Engine<br /></strong>The Claims Engine team powers Grow’s end-to-end insurance claim lifecycle, from claim creation through submission, remits, and denials. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build robust, observable services that encode complex payor rules, reduce denials and rework, and ensure providers get paid accurately and on time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Role Details:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$182,000 - $250,000 USD Annually.</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nWe're hiring a Software Engineer to help build and evolve the backend systems that power Grow Therapy's platform. In this role, you'll design, implement, and ship server-side features and services that directly impact how clients and providers connect, communicate, and access care.\n\nYou'll join a collaborative, product-focused engineering organization where technical work is closely tied to reliability, scalability, and real-world outcomes. This role is ideal for an engineer who takes pride in writing clean, well-tested code, thinks carefully about system design and data integrity, and is energized by the opportunity to grow alongside a fast-moving team.\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS\n\nAccess to mental healthcare in America is still deeply fragmented and Grow Therapy is building the platform to fix that. We connect clients, providers, and health plans in a single integrated system, and the software our engineers ship directly shapes whether people can find and afford the care they need.\n\nWe're growing fast - nearly 22,000 clinicians, over 1.4 million clients, and on track to surpass 10 million sessions in 2026 and we see ourselves as a generational company with a long way still to go. Engineers who join now have a real opportunity to build systems that matter at meaningful scale.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Own backend services and APIs end to end — from technical design through implementation, deployment, and ongoing reliability\n\n - Drive architectural decisions within your team, bringing structure and clarity to complex, ambiguous problem spaces\n\n - Lead improvements to core platform systems, including data pipelines, service reliability, and business logic\n\n - Design and enable safe, repeatable experimentation through robust A/B testing and analysis workflows\n\n - Diagnose and resolve data quality, performance, and correctness issues across systems\n\n - Write clean, well-tested, maintainable production code and set a high bar through code reviews and technical mentorship\n\n - Partner closely with Product, Design, and Data to translate goals into technical designs and execution plans\n\n - Shape the technical direction of your team and contribute meaningfully to cross-team architectural discussions\n\n\nYOU'LL BE A GOOD FIT IF YOU HAVE\n\n - 7+ years of professional software engineering experience with meaningful ownership of production backend systems\n\n - Deep backend engineering expertise, including service design, data modeling, and API development at scale\n\n - Experience building and operating systems where reliability, data quality, and performance are critical\n\n - Proven ability to operate in ambiguous problem spaces and drive clarity across technical and cross-functional stakeholders\n\n - A highly data-driven mindset, comfortable with experimentation, measurement, and optimization from both product and technical perspectives\n\n - A product-minded approach — you understand how technical decisions impact user experience and business outcomes\n\n - Strong collaboration and communication skills, with a track record of influencing cross-functional partners including Product, Design, and Data Science\n\n - Experience using AI-assisted dev tools (e.g., Cursor, GitHub Copilot)\n\n - A bias toward ownership, speed, learning, and continuous improvement\n\n\nENGINEERING TEAM OVERVIEWS\n\nMarketplace Experience\nThe Marketplace Experience team shapes how clients discover and evaluate providers on Grow, transforming a simple directory into a guided, personalized entry point to care. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll work across search, ranking, profiles, and booking flows to build a fast, resilient, and intelligent marketplace that helps every client find the right fit provider and convert that intent into a booked appointment.\n\nClient Activation\nThe Client Activation team owns the fragile moments between booking and a client’s first few sessions, making starting care feel clear, reliable, and supportive. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build and harden systems for scheduling, authentication, notifications, and early-journey flows that directly determine whether clients show up, come back for visit two, and build lasting relationships with their providers.\n\nClaims Engine\nThe Claims Engine team powers Grow’s end-to-end insurance claim lifecycle, from claim creation through submission, remits, and denials. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build robust, observable services that encode complex payor rules, reduce denials and rework, and ensure providers get paid accurately and on time.\n\nRole Details:\n\n - Employment Type: Full Time, Exempt \n\n - Base Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $182,000 - $250,000 USD Annually.\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d4732124-9e19-47dd-8fdd-c37cffbeaadc","title":"Senior Software Engineer - Full Stack","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-30T19:01:07.925+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d4732124-9e19-47dd-8fdd-c37cffbeaadc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d4732124-9e19-47dd-8fdd-c37cffbeaadc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring a Full Stack Senior Software Engineer to help build and evolve the systems that power Grow Therapy's platform. In this role, you'll work across the stack to design, implement, and ship features that directly impact how clients and providers connect, communicate, and access care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll join a collaborative, product-focused engineering organization where technical work is closely tied to learning, iteration, and real-world outcomes. This role is ideal for an engineer who takes pride in writing clean, maintainable code, thinks deeply about system behavior, and is energized by the opportunity to grow alongside a fast-moving team.</p><h2><strong>Why This Role Matters</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Access to mental healthcare in America is still deeply fragmented and Grow Therapy is building the platform to fix that. We connect clients, providers, and health plans in a single integrated system, and the software our engineers ship directly shapes whether people can find and afford the care they need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're growing fast - nearly 22,000 clinicians, over 1.4 million clients, and on track to surpass 10 million sessions in 2026 and we see ourselves as a generational company with a long way still to go. Engineers who join now have a real opportunity to build systems that matter at meaningful scale.</p><h2><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and ship customer-facing features that span frontend and backend systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the full lifecycle of your work - from scoping and implementation through testing, deployment, and iteration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to and improve core platform systems, including those related to discovery, scheduling, transactions, and user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement and support A/B tests and experiments, from hypothesis through measurement and rollout</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate, triage, and resolve production incidents and complex cross-system bugs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, well-tested, maintainable production code and take an active role in code reviews</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Product, Design, and Data to deliver well-scoped, measurable solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in technical discussions and contribute to architectural decisions within your team</p></li></ul><h2><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If You Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>6+ years</strong> of professional software engineering experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and maintaining production systems at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working across backend APIs and frontend interfaces, with hands-on experience in <strong>Python</strong> and modern <strong>React/TypeScript</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on systems where data quality, correctness, and performance matter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong execution skills and the ability to deliver scoped work independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity and a willingness to learn complex systems and new problem domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A product-minded approach - you understand how technical decisions impact user experience and business outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong collaboration and communication skills, with a track record of working closely with cross-functional partners including Product, Design, and Data Science</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using AI-assisted dev tools (e.g., Claude, Cursor)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward ownership, speed, learning, and continuous improvement</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Team Descriptions</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>New Markets &amp; Model - </strong> The New Markets &amp; Models team drives Grow’s next phase of growth by validating and scaling new business models and complex partnerships. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build the flexible, greenfield systems that power early-stage referral channels, novel reimbursement structures, and experimental care models before they become part of the core platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Quality</strong> - The Care Quality team builds the data and workflows Grow uses to prove and improve the clinical quality of care to payors and partners. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll develop systems that capture measures, structure documentation, and surface insights so we can demonstrate outcomes and power value-based partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Client Activation</strong> – The Client Activation team owns the fragile moments between booking and a client’s first few sessions, making starting care feel clear, reliable, and supportive. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build and harden systems for scheduling, authentication, notifications, and early-journey flows that directly determine whether clients show up, come back for visit two, and build lasting relationships with their providers</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Client Engagement</strong>  - The Client Engagement team owns the experiences that keep clients connected between and across sessions—web and app surfaces, notifications, and core journeys. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll ship features that help clients stay on track with care plans, manage appointments, and stay engaged long after their first visit.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Coverage &amp; Payments Experience </strong>- The Payments Experience team owns the client-facing financial journey, from eligibility checks and cost estimates to charging cards and handling balances. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build systems that make insurance coverage understandable, reduce billing surprises, and keep the money flow trustworthy for both clients and providers.<strong><br /></strong></p><h2><strong>Role Details</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$182,000–$250,000 USD Annually.</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nWe're hiring a Full Stack Senior Software Engineer to help build and evolve the systems that power Grow Therapy's platform. In this role, you'll work across the stack to design, implement, and ship features that directly impact how clients and providers connect, communicate, and access care.\n\nYou'll join a collaborative, product-focused engineering organization where technical work is closely tied to learning, iteration, and real-world outcomes. This role is ideal for an engineer who takes pride in writing clean, maintainable code, thinks deeply about system behavior, and is energized by the opportunity to grow alongside a fast-moving team.\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS\n\nAccess to mental healthcare in America is still deeply fragmented and Grow Therapy is building the platform to fix that. We connect clients, providers, and health plans in a single integrated system, and the software our engineers ship directly shapes whether people can find and afford the care they need.\n\nWe're growing fast - nearly 22,000 clinicians, over 1.4 million clients, and on track to surpass 10 million sessions in 2026 and we see ourselves as a generational company with a long way still to go. Engineers who join now have a real opportunity to build systems that matter at meaningful scale.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Design, implement, and ship customer-facing features that span frontend and backend systems\n\n - Own the full lifecycle of your work - from scoping and implementation through testing, deployment, and iteration\n\n - Contribute to and improve core platform systems, including those related to discovery, scheduling, transactions, and user experience\n\n - Implement and support A/B tests and experiments, from hypothesis through measurement and rollout\n\n - Investigate, triage, and resolve production incidents and complex cross-system bugs\n\n - Write clean, well-tested, maintainable production code and take an active role in code reviews\n\n - Collaborate closely with Product, Design, and Data to deliver well-scoped, measurable solutions\n\n - Participate in technical discussions and contribute to architectural decisions within your team\n\n\nYOU'LL BE A GOOD FIT IF YOU HAVE\n\n - 6+ years of professional software engineering experience\n\n - Experience building and maintaining production systems at scale\n\n - Comfortable working across backend APIs and frontend interfaces, with hands-on experience in Python and modern React/TypeScript\n\n - Experience working on systems where data quality, correctness, and performance matter\n\n - Strong execution skills and the ability to deliver scoped work independently\n\n - Curiosity and a willingness to learn complex systems and new problem domains\n\n - A product-minded approach - you understand how technical decisions impact user experience and business outcomes\n\n - Strong collaboration and communication skills, with a track record of working closely with cross-functional partners including Product, Design, and Data Science\n\n - Experience using AI-assisted dev tools (e.g., Claude, Cursor)\n\n - A bias toward ownership, speed, learning, and continuous improvement\n\n\nTEAM DESCRIPTIONS\n\nNew Markets & Model -  The New Markets & Models team drives Grow’s next phase of growth by validating and scaling new business models and complex partnerships. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build the flexible, greenfield systems that power early-stage referral channels, novel reimbursement structures, and experimental care models before they become part of the core platform.\n\nCare Quality - The Care Quality team builds the data and workflows Grow uses to prove and improve the clinical quality of care to payors and partners. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll develop systems that capture measures, structure documentation, and surface insights so we can demonstrate outcomes and power value-based partnerships.\n\nClient Activation – The Client Activation team owns the fragile moments between booking and a client’s first few sessions, making starting care feel clear, reliable, and supportive. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build and harden systems for scheduling, authentication, notifications, and early-journey flows that directly determine whether clients show up, come back for visit two, and build lasting relationships with their providers\n\nClient Engagement  - The Client Engagement team owns the experiences that keep clients connected between and across sessions—web and app surfaces, notifications, and core journeys. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll ship features that help clients stay on track with care plans, manage appointments, and stay engaged long after their first visit.\n\nCoverage & Payments Experience - The Payments Experience team owns the client-facing financial journey, from eligibility checks and cost estimates to charging cards and handling balances. As a Software Engineer on this team, you’ll build systems that make insurance coverage understandable, reduce billing surprises, and keep the money flow trustworthy for both clients and providers.\n\n\n\nROLE DETAILS\n\n - Employment Type: Full Time, Exempt \n\n - Base Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $182,000–$250,000 USD Annually.\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"058d3dd1-c7c7-421d-9ede-e7f9afdb6211","title":"Senior Software Engineer - Developer Experience & AI Enablement ","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-31T14:47:27.777+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/058d3dd1-c7c7-421d-9ede-e7f9afdb6211","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/058d3dd1-c7c7-421d-9ede-e7f9afdb6211/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Senior AI Enablement Engineer to join the Product Infrastructure team at Grow Therapy and help define how AI transforms the way we work across the entire organization. You will design and build the foundational AI infrastructure, tooling, and workflows that enable every department to operate more efficiently and effectively. You will be part of a hub-based team in San Francisco.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your responsibilities will include building scalable AI systems, partnering cross-functionally with Engineering, Operations, Finance, Legal, and People teams, and driving measurable adoption of AI-powered workflows company-wide.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement Grow's internal AI control plane and tooling ecosystem, including MCPs, AI skills frameworks, and secure connectors to internal systems such as our code, data warehouses, CRMs, finance tools, and internal databases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build autonomous agents that can solve common classes of engineering problems (feature building, design changes, refactors, tech debt, bug triage, log analysis, etc)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reusable, production-ready AI workflows and department-specific copilots that reduce manual effort and accelerate decision-making across teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct deep workflow discovery sessions with cross-functional partners to identify high-leverage AI opportunities that drive measurable business value</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Security, Legal, and Data teams to ensure all AI infrastructure is compliant, secure, and aligned with data governance standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide documentation, enablement sessions, and feedback loops to drive adoption, and establish metrics to track efficiency gains and platform reliability</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 5+ years of experience in software engineering, platform engineering, or infrastructure roles with hands-on experience building AI-enabled systems (LLMs, skills, MCPs, orchestration frameworks, etc)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience designing and maintaining internal platforms, APIs, or developer tooling and are energized by improving developer experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a strong cross-functional collaborator who can translate business workflows into well-designed technical systems and communicate effectively with non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You bring experience with security, data governance, and reliability best practices in production systems, ideally in regulated or healthcare-adjacent environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have familiarity with AI agent frameworks, tool/skills registries, MCPs, or experience integrating enterprise systems (CRM, HRIS, finance tools, ticketing systems)</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt (or Non-Exempt)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$200,000–$250,000 USD Annually</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our San Francisco or Seattle hub locations <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nWe are looking for a Senior AI Enablement Engineer to join the Product Infrastructure team at Grow Therapy and help define how AI transforms the way we work across the entire organization. You will design and build the foundational AI infrastructure, tooling, and workflows that enable every department to operate more efficiently and effectively. You will be part of a hub-based team in San Francisco.\n\nYour responsibilities will include building scalable AI systems, partnering cross-functionally with Engineering, Operations, Finance, Legal, and People teams, and driving measurable adoption of AI-powered workflows company-wide.\n\nWhat You'll Be Doing:\n\n - Design and implement Grow's internal AI control plane and tooling ecosystem, including MCPs, AI skills frameworks, and secure connectors to internal systems such as our code, data warehouses, CRMs, finance tools, and internal databases\n\n - Build autonomous agents that can solve common classes of engineering problems (feature building, design changes, refactors, tech debt, bug triage, log analysis, etc)\n\n - Build reusable, production-ready AI workflows and department-specific copilots that reduce manual effort and accelerate decision-making across teams\n\n - Conduct deep workflow discovery sessions with cross-functional partners to identify high-leverage AI opportunities that drive measurable business value\n\n - Partner with Security, Legal, and Data teams to ensure all AI infrastructure is compliant, secure, and aligned with data governance standards\n\n - Provide documentation, enablement sessions, and feedback loops to drive adoption, and establish metrics to track efficiency gains and platform reliability\n\nYou'll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have 5+ years of experience in software engineering, platform engineering, or infrastructure roles with hands-on experience building AI-enabled systems (LLMs, skills, MCPs, orchestration frameworks, etc)\n\n - You have experience designing and maintaining internal platforms, APIs, or developer tooling and are energized by improving developer experience\n\n - You are a strong cross-functional collaborator who can translate business workflows into well-designed technical systems and communicate effectively with non-technical stakeholders\n\n - You bring experience with security, data governance, and reliability best practices in production systems, ideally in regulated or healthcare-adjacent environments\n\n - You have familiarity with AI agent frameworks, tool/skills registries, MCPs, or experience integrating enterprise systems (CRM, HRIS, finance tools, ticketing systems)\n\n \n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt (or Non-Exempt)\n\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $200,000–$250,000 USD Annually\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our San Francisco or Seattle hub locations three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$182K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$182K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c1da25f2-0cab-4e51-a322-83dc9950a2eb","tierSummary":"$182K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"91c59073-072b-4f38-aee1-74811d90ef5e","summary":"$182K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"8de88391-5125-490c-b2d5-4b7cdf8e9e70","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"9b01902d-8fb7-4085-a0c2-7dd85e10a8a9","title":"Staff Product Manager, Patient Experience (Payments)","department":"Technology","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-05T15:12:11.797+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/9b01902d-8fb7-4085-a0c2-7dd85e10a8a9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/9b01902d-8fb7-4085-a0c2-7dd85e10a8a9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role: </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">One of the biggest barriers to accessing mental health care today is cost uncertainty and financial constraints. As the Product Manager for Grow’s new Billing Experience team, you will own a charter focused on building a best-in-class experience that gives clients confidence to start and continue care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will define the product vision and lead a roadmap that transforms one of the most frustrating aspects of healthcare into a meaningful differentiator for Grow. This is an opportunity to turn complexity into clarity and create an experience that clients trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working closely with engineering, design, data, and operations, you will have the strategic ownership to define what best-in-class truly means in a space where no competitor has fully solved the problem.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the roadmap and strategy for our Payments Experience team, building an experience that makes using insurance and paying for care a delightful experience for clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with our UXR, Design, Client Support, and Data teams to identify the main opportunities for improvement in our billing experience as it relates to insurance and payments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In collaboration with our Design team, define and deliver an end to end experience that removes friction across insurance and payments while translating complex concepts such as deductibles and coverage changes into clear, intuitive, and actionable experiences for clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Launch innovative features with a meaningful and measurable impact to client retention and experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product experience: 5+ years in a product management role where you owned the full strategy of your end-to-end surface area.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Innovative mindset - you’ve launched 0-1 features before in a high ambiguity space.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills and a comfort with data analysis and experimentation; you make decisions with data and know how to use data to uncover user needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong prioritization instincts: You know how to balance short-term wins with long-term platform investments and focus on what drives the most impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">User empathy: You enjoy talking to users and translating real pain points into thoughtful product solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptability: You’re comfortable navigating ambiguity, learning quickly, and adjusting as new information emerges.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams and deliver impactful products in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence across levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of owning outcomes, not just outputs — you care about whether the thing you shipped actually moved the needle.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nAbout the Role: \n\nOne of the biggest barriers to accessing mental health care today is cost uncertainty and financial constraints. As the Product Manager for Grow’s new Billing Experience team, you will own a charter focused on building a best-in-class experience that gives clients confidence to start and continue care.\n\nYou will define the product vision and lead a roadmap that transforms one of the most frustrating aspects of healthcare into a meaningful differentiator for Grow. This is an opportunity to turn complexity into clarity and create an experience that clients trust.\n\nWorking closely with engineering, design, data, and operations, you will have the strategic ownership to define what best-in-class truly means in a space where no competitor has fully solved the problem.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Own the roadmap and strategy for our Payments Experience team, building an experience that makes using insurance and paying for care a delightful experience for clients.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with our UXR, Design, Client Support, and Data teams to identify the main opportunities for improvement in our billing experience as it relates to insurance and payments.\n\n - In collaboration with our Design team, define and deliver an end to end experience that removes friction across insurance and payments while translating complex concepts such as deductibles and coverage changes into clear, intuitive, and actionable experiences for clients.\n\n - Launch innovative features with a meaningful and measurable impact to client retention and experience.\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - Product experience: 5+ years in a product management role where you owned the full strategy of your end-to-end surface area.\n\n - Innovative mindset - you’ve launched 0-1 features before in a high ambiguity space.\n\n - Strong analytical skills and a comfort with data analysis and experimentation; you make decisions with data and know how to use data to uncover user needs\n\n - Strong prioritization instincts: You know how to balance short-term wins with long-term platform investments and focus on what drives the most impact.\n\n - User empathy: You enjoy talking to users and translating real pain points into thoughtful product solutions.\n\n - Adaptability: You’re comfortable navigating ambiguity, learning quickly, and adjusting as new information emerges.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams and deliver impactful products in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence across levels.\n\n - A track record of owning outcomes, not just outputs — you care about whether the thing you shipped actually moved the needle.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"8f91158c-2825-459d-95fb-c9d3ca312f12","tierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5f31aaa9-7054-4624-bf5b-b313f0ac07c2","summary":"$200K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"39af5766-05df-435f-a284-01577bb309d1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e147bc25-009b-40b2-ad02-2f8a957a7398","title":"Commercial Strategy Senior Manager","department":"Business","team":"Strategic Partnerships","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T22:22:59.344+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/e147bc25-009b-40b2-ad02-2f8a957a7398","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/e147bc25-009b-40b2-ad02-2f8a957a7398/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow Therapy works with most of the largest health plans in the country. As those relationships have matured, the interesting question has shifted from whether a plan works with us to what we should build together, and there is no standard answer to that question.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns a focused set of key relationships end to end. You decide what should be built with each plan, design the structure that delivers it, negotiate it, and stay with it once it is live.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The work runs on a multi-year horizon. You will spend real time with health plans’ senior executives, enough that they bring you problems before they have decided what to do about them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with our Director, Payor Strategy and our VP, Corporate and Business Development on a team small enough that each person carries a meaningful share of the company's strategy and influence to drive it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deciding what to build</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a point of view on each health plan you cover: where their behavioral health strategy is heading, what is not working, who owns the problem internally, and what would need to be true for them to commit to something ambitious.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design the solution from first principles including economics, complex deal terms, directed volume, integrated referral pathways, co-developed clinical programs, risk-sharing. The right combination differs by plan, and in most cases it does not exist anywhere in the market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the analytical case. Size the opportunity, model the economics, test the assumptions, and produce work that holds up to a health plan's strategy and finance teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with Grow’s leadership. Work closely with our co-founders, operations, product, engineering, and finance to assist in the build, negotiation, and execution of the partnership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Structuring and landing it</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the commercial structuring, including rate design, exclusivity mechanics, volume commitments, and performance economics, in direct conversation with health plan executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the relationships that make ambitious structures possible. Agreements of this scope are approved by a small number of senior people at each plan, and reaching them takes sustained time and credibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring Grow's operations, product, clinical, and finance teams into what you are designing, making the trade-offs required to turn a novel structure into something we can deliver.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Owning what it produces</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay with the partnership after launch. Track how it is performing, work out why/when it is not, and use your relationships with health plan leaders to adjust the structure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply what you learn in-market to the next structure, both with that plan and with the others you cover.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feed what you learn back into Grow's product roadmap and long-range planning.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have three to seven years of experience in strategy consulting, corporate development, private equity, venture capital, or a strategy function at a high-growth company, with a record of strong performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are comfortable with problems that have no established approach, and you tend to spend real time on how a problem is structured before solving it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You want to see your work through. Designing the structure is the interesting part, and you also care about how it performs once it is in-market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can hold your own with senior external executives and build long-term relationships with them. You lead with the answer, and you build arguments that work on sophisticated audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You think through second-order effects, including how a proposal lands across a health plan's network, actuarial, and clinical teams, and what it commits Grow to operationally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You build the plan rather than asking for one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare experience is helpful but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt<br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> <strong>$161,000–$215,000 USD Annually</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: $134,000–$179,167 USD Annually </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role can be <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>) or <strong>fully remote.</strong> Both arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nGrow Therapy works with most of the largest health plans in the country. As those relationships have matured, the interesting question has shifted from whether a plan works with us to what we should build together, and there is no standard answer to that question.\n\nThis role owns a focused set of key relationships end to end. You decide what should be built with each plan, design the structure that delivers it, negotiate it, and stay with it once it is live.\n\nThe work runs on a multi-year horizon. You will spend real time with health plans’ senior executives, enough that they bring you problems before they have decided what to do about them.\n\nYou will work closely with our Director, Payor Strategy and our VP, Corporate and Business Development on a team small enough that each person carries a meaningful share of the company's strategy and influence to drive it.\n\nWhat You'll Be Doing\n\nDeciding what to build\n\n - Develop a point of view on each health plan you cover: where their behavioral health strategy is heading, what is not working, who owns the problem internally, and what would need to be true for them to commit to something ambitious.\n\n - Design the solution from first principles including economics, complex deal terms, directed volume, integrated referral pathways, co-developed clinical programs, risk-sharing. The right combination differs by plan, and in most cases it does not exist anywhere in the market.\n\n - Build the analytical case. Size the opportunity, model the economics, test the assumptions, and produce work that holds up to a health plan's strategy and finance teams.\n\n - Coordinate with Grow’s leadership. Work closely with our co-founders, operations, product, engineering, and finance to assist in the build, negotiation, and execution of the partnership.\n\nStructuring and landing it\n\n - Lead the commercial structuring, including rate design, exclusivity mechanics, volume commitments, and performance economics, in direct conversation with health plan executives.\n\n - Build the relationships that make ambitious structures possible. Agreements of this scope are approved by a small number of senior people at each plan, and reaching them takes sustained time and credibility.\n\n - Bring Grow's operations, product, clinical, and finance teams into what you are designing, making the trade-offs required to turn a novel structure into something we can deliver.\n\nOwning what it produces\n\n - Stay with the partnership after launch. Track how it is performing, work out why/when it is not, and use your relationships with health plan leaders to adjust the structure.\n\n - Apply what you learn in-market to the next structure, both with that plan and with the others you cover.\n\n - Feed what you learn back into Grow's product roadmap and long-range planning.\n\nYou'll Be a Good Fit If\n\n - You have three to seven years of experience in strategy consulting, corporate development, private equity, venture capital, or a strategy function at a high-growth company, with a record of strong performance.\n\n - You are comfortable with problems that have no established approach, and you tend to spend real time on how a problem is structured before solving it.\n\n - You want to see your work through. Designing the structure is the interesting part, and you also care about how it performs once it is in-market.\n\n - You can hold your own with senior external executives and build long-term relationships with them. You lead with the answer, and you build arguments that work on sophisticated audiences.\n\n - You think through second-order effects, including how a proposal lands across a health plan's network, actuarial, and clinical teams, and what it commits Grow to operationally.\n\n - You build the plan rather than asking for one.\n\n - Healthcare experience is helpful but not required.\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is\n\nHybrid Commitment: $161,000–$215,000 USD Annually\n\nFully Remote Commitment: $134,000–$179,167 USD Annually \n\nThis role can be hybrid (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday) or fully remote. Both arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$134K – $215K • Offers Equity • Multiple Ranges","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$134,000 - $215,000","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6559b8dc-fde0-49cd-9c52-a1ba72dfff7f","tierSummary":"Estimated Base Salary $134,000 – $179,167 • Offers Equity","title":"Remote","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"67593a22-9ded-46fe-a146-588ef365e526","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fb8ff171-462b-4c5c-9dbc-5a42e53ee6a5","summary":"Estimated Base Salary $134,000 – $179,167","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":134000,"maxValue":179167}]},{"id":"c9d94f75-9dde-451b-a1ab-948b6ec01a0f","tierSummary":"Estimated Base Salary $161,000 – $215,000 • Offers Equity","title":"Hybrid","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"033de391-3652-4eb1-b0c5-0a3876eed3d9","summary":"Estimated Base Salary $161,000 – $215,000","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161000,"maxValue":215000},{"id":"94d5defa-3d2d-4eed-b1ad-29f96f04d1c8","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","minValue":null,"maxValue":null,"interval":"1 YEAR"},{"minValue":134000,"maxValue":215000,"currencyCode":"USD","interval":"1 YEAR","compensationType":"Salary"}]}},{"id":"7c1a3ad0-985a-4b66-85f4-910d8e8256ec","title":"Engineering Manager, AI Enablement","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-11T15:41:22.895+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/7c1a3ad0-985a-4b66-85f4-910d8e8256ec","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/7c1a3ad0-985a-4b66-85f4-910d8e8256ec/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for an Engineering Manager to lead Grow's newly formed AI Enablement Tech Team, the central engine behind the company's AI strategy. Alongside a dedicated PM, you'll own the company-wide AI roadmap, build the foundational infrastructure every function depends on, and drive end-to-end delivery of our most complex AI use cases. You'll lead a executive-aligned engineering team and run an ongoing cross-functional working group with AI Champions across the organization. This is a rare opportunity to define how AI works at Grow, not just for engineering, but for the entire company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the technical strategy and execution of Grow's company-wide AI roadmap, sequencing infrastructure investments and use cases against company-level impact in close partnership with the PM</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operate core AI infrastructure: data pipelines, model access, embeddings, retrieval layers, and governance frameworks, with PHI compliance as a non-negotiable constraint</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and maintain the connector layer (MCPs, integrations, and APIs) that enables agentic workflows across every business function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead delivery of high-priority, complex AI use cases requiring close Product and Engineering collaboration (e.g. Grow LLM, AI-assisted care workflows)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive AI vendor governance: procurement decisions, contracts, and a cross-company tool registry that prevents redundant spend and ungoverned tooling</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 8+ years of software engineering experience with 5+ years leading engineering teams, including hands-on experience building AI/ML infrastructure, LLM-powered systems, or agentic workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have strong technical depth in AI/ML infrastructure: you've built or operated pipelines, embedding systems, retrieval layers, or orchestration frameworks in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You bring excellent cross-functional leadership: you're equally effective in a technical design review and a working group with clinical, legal, or business stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You operate with a founder's mindset: you bring structure to ambiguity, move fast, and build systems designed to scale beyond your direct involvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're a strong communicator who can translate technical decisions into clear business impact for senior leadership and non-technical partners</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nWe're looking for an Engineering Manager to lead Grow's newly formed AI Enablement Tech Team, the central engine behind the company's AI strategy. Alongside a dedicated PM, you'll own the company-wide AI roadmap, build the foundational infrastructure every function depends on, and drive end-to-end delivery of our most complex AI use cases. You'll lead a executive-aligned engineering team and run an ongoing cross-functional working group with AI Champions across the organization. This is a rare opportunity to define how AI works at Grow, not just for engineering, but for the entire company.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Own the technical strategy and execution of Grow's company-wide AI roadmap, sequencing infrastructure investments and use cases against company-level impact in close partnership with the PM\n\n - Build and operate core AI infrastructure: data pipelines, model access, embeddings, retrieval layers, and governance frameworks, with PHI compliance as a non-negotiable constraint\n\n - Architect and maintain the connector layer (MCPs, integrations, and APIs) that enables agentic workflows across every business function\n\n - Lead delivery of high-priority, complex AI use cases requiring close Product and Engineering collaboration (e.g. Grow LLM, AI-assisted care workflows)\n\n - Drive AI vendor governance: procurement decisions, contracts, and a cross-company tool registry that prevents redundant spend and ungoverned tooling\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have 8+ years of software engineering experience with 5+ years leading engineering teams, including hands-on experience building AI/ML infrastructure, LLM-powered systems, or agentic workflows\n\n - You have strong technical depth in AI/ML infrastructure: you've built or operated pipelines, embedding systems, retrieval layers, or orchestration frameworks in production\n\n - You bring excellent cross-functional leadership: you're equally effective in a technical design review and a working group with clinical, legal, or business stakeholders\n\n - You operate with a founder's mindset: you bring structure to ambiguity, move fast, and build systems designed to scale beyond your direct involvement\n\n - You're a strong communicator who can translate technical decisions into clear business impact for senior leadership and non-technical partners\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$225K – $300K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$225K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b86578c3-1aa0-42e0-8646-11d297cbebca","tierSummary":"$225K – $300K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0cfea4dc-40eb-4553-af63-54c89edacd27","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cbf7e52f-f851-4616-9b2d-b9da1ce03ae6","summary":"$225K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":225000,"maxValue":300000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":225000,"maxValue":300000}]}},{"id":"08b049ac-7918-4a0f-8574-2e8e44513b7c","title":"Specialist II, Release of Information Operations","department":"Business","team":"Insurance Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T19:33:22.318+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/08b049ac-7918-4a0f-8574-2e8e44513b7c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/08b049ac-7918-4a0f-8574-2e8e44513b7c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an experienced Release of Information (ROI) Specialist who is passionate about improving the landscape for mental healthcare. You will be responsible for responding to all types of ROI requests, ranging in scope and scale, to support the needs of our clients, payors, and other requesters. You'll be joining our remote-friendly team of ROI Specialists, reporting directly to the ROI Operations Manager, with an ROI Operations Supervisor overseeing day-to-day operations — contributing to a team that's growing to meet the needs of an ever-expanding client and provider community.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing: </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process, log, and respond to inbound medical record requests from clients, insurance companies, attorneys, and other valid requesters within required timeframes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and validate request documents, authorizations, subpoenas, and records for production to ensure that all releases are accurate, complete, and in compliance with federal and state regulations, HIPAA, and other relevant privacy laws governing the release of mental health information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain strict confidentiality and safeguard all patient information in accordance with privacy regulations and company policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with clients, Grow providers, and other requesters to clarify or obtain additional information, assist with their records needs, and provide status updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with teammates on special projects including broader chart audits, and serve as a resource to other Grow teams with ROI or records questions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If You: </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years experience in Release of Information or medical records management </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health information management education and/or credentials are a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are tech savvy, adept at navigating EMRs and other systems, tools, and ticketing software to track work and communicate with teammates and customers </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are a team player, adaptable, collaborative by nature, and keen to cultivate positive customer experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have great attention to detail and an eye for process improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in mental/behavioral health and/or tech is a plus (but not required)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Non-Exempt<br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$25.00 - $26.44 USD per hour).<br /></strong>This is a <strong>remote role</strong> with the expectation to travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWe are looking for an experienced Release of Information (ROI) Specialist who is passionate about improving the landscape for mental healthcare. You will be responsible for responding to all types of ROI requests, ranging in scope and scale, to support the needs of our clients, payors, and other requesters. You'll be joining our remote-friendly team of ROI Specialists, reporting directly to the ROI Operations Manager, with an ROI Operations Supervisor overseeing day-to-day operations — contributing to a team that's growing to meet the needs of an ever-expanding client and provider community.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing: \n\n - Process, log, and respond to inbound medical record requests from clients, insurance companies, attorneys, and other valid requesters within required timeframes\n\n - Review and validate request documents, authorizations, subpoenas, and records for production to ensure that all releases are accurate, complete, and in compliance with federal and state regulations, HIPAA, and other relevant privacy laws governing the release of mental health information\n\n - Maintain strict confidentiality and safeguard all patient information in accordance with privacy regulations and company policy\n\n - Communicate with clients, Grow providers, and other requesters to clarify or obtain additional information, assist with their records needs, and provide status updates\n\n - Collaborate with teammates on special projects including broader chart audits, and serve as a resource to other Grow teams with ROI or records questions\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If You: \n\n - 2+ years experience in Release of Information or medical records management \n\n - Health information management education and/or credentials are a plus\n\n - Are tech savvy, adept at navigating EMRs and other systems, tools, and ticketing software to track work and communicate with teammates and customers \n\n - Are a team player, adaptable, collaborative by nature, and keen to cultivate positive customer experiences\n\n - Have great attention to detail and an eye for process improvement\n\n - Experience in mental/behavioral health and/or tech is a plus (but not required)\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Non-Exempt\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $25.00 - $26.44 USD per hour).\nThis is a remote role with the expectation to travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$25.00 – $26.44 per hour • Fully Remote Commitment","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"bf1b7100-7d79-45ae-9d1d-29f4560d8f5e","tierSummary":"$25.00 – $26.44 per hour • Fully Remote Commitment","title":null,"additionalInformation":"Fully Remote Commitment","components":[{"id":"6dabbeb4-45d5-47ca-888d-545ebc4797aa","summary":"$25.00 – $26.44 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":26.44}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":26.44}]}},{"id":"dbb244c2-08aa-44f9-b695-4c97d73a7b4a","title":"Senior Platform Reliability Engineer","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T21:08:20.537+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/dbb244c2-08aa-44f9-b695-4c97d73a7b4a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/dbb244c2-08aa-44f9-b695-4c97d73a7b4a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring a<strong> Senior Platform Reliability Engineer </strong>to help define and scale reliability as a first-class capability at Grow. In this role you’ll operate horizontally across the organization, shaping how reliability is understood, measured, and built into the developer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll work closely with other members of the platform team as well as our product engineering teams to establish standards around observability, SLOs/SLAs, and incident response—while also helping translate those standards into self-service tooling and “golden paths” that make it easy for teams to adopt them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-impact, highly autonomous role where you’ll drive both cultural and technical change, ultimately enabling teams to independently build and operate reliable systems at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll help us establish and scale  reliability as a discipline at Grow by:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Defining Reliability Standards </strong>Establishing frameworks for SLOs/SLAs, error budgets, and operational readiness; helping teams understand what to measure and why it matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Improving Observability &amp; Measurement </strong>Identifying gaps in metrics, logging, and tracing; ensuring services are measurable, debuggable, and aligned with reliability goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evolving Incident Response </strong>Developing and improving incident response practices, from detection to post-incident learning, and helping teams build sustainable on-call and escalation patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enabling Self-Service Reliability </strong>Partnering with the platform team to build tooling and abstractions (e.g., service scorecards, dashboards, templates, golden paths) that make it easy for teams to adopt and stay compliant with reliability standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Driving Adoption Across Teams </strong>Working cross-functionally to educate, influence, and guide engineering teams—scaling reliability practices through a combination of clear standards, strong communication, and developer-friendly systems</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experienced in production systems:</strong> You have 6+ years of experience operating and improving reliability of production systems at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong foundation in cloud and infrastructure:</strong> You have hands-on experience with AWS, Kubernetes (e.g., EKS), and infrastructure as code tools like Terraform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep understanding of reliability principles:</strong> You’ve defined or worked with SLOs/SLAs, understand error budgets, and have experience improving reliability through measurement and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Observability expertise:</strong> You’ve worked with modern observability tooling (we use DataDog) and understand how to build actionable monitoring systems across metrics, logs, and traces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems thinker:</strong> You’re able to zoom out, identify patterns across teams and services, and design solutions that scale beyond a single system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Impact-oriented:</strong> You focus on outcomes over output and care deeply about improving real reliability outcomes—not just adding processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong communicator and influencer:</strong> You can drive change across teams without direct authority, balancing pragmatism with long-term vision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Self-directed:</strong> You thrive in ambiguous environments and are comfortable defining problems, proposing solutions, and executing independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team player</strong>: You collaborate well, communicate with empathy, and enjoy mentoring and learning from others.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Points</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve helped introduce or scale reliability practices in a growing organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve built internal tooling or platforms used by multiple teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience designing service-level scorecards or compliance/reporting systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve worked with both SaaS (e.g., DataDog) and self-managed observability stacks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You were previously a product engineer and bring empathy for developer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience with database reliability and performance (we use PostgreSQL)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why This Role Is Exciting</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to define what reliability looks like at a growing, scaling engineering organization—and to do it in a way that actually sticks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You won’t just be responding to incidents or working within a single team. You’ll be shaping how reliability is measured, enforced, and experienced across the entire company. You’ll work alongside your team mates to turn best practices into intuitive, self-service systems that engineers rely on every day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your work will directly improve system reliability, reduce incidents, and enable teams to move faster with confidence, ultimately making reliability a built-in property of how we build software at Grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Role Details</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$182,000–$250,000 USD Annually.</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our San Francisco, NYC, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe’re hiring a Senior Platform Reliability Engineer to help define and scale reliability as a first-class capability at Grow. In this role you’ll operate horizontally across the organization, shaping how reliability is understood, measured, and built into the developer experience.\n\nYou’ll work closely with other members of the platform team as well as our product engineering teams to establish standards around observability, SLOs/SLAs, and incident response—while also helping translate those standards into self-service tooling and “golden paths” that make it easy for teams to adopt them.\n\nThis is a high-impact, highly autonomous role where you’ll drive both cultural and technical change, ultimately enabling teams to independently build and operate reliable systems at scale.\n\n\n\nWhat You'll Work On\n\nYou’ll help us establish and scale  reliability as a discipline at Grow by:\n\n - Defining Reliability Standards Establishing frameworks for SLOs/SLAs, error budgets, and operational readiness; helping teams understand what to measure and why it matters.\n\n - Improving Observability & Measurement Identifying gaps in metrics, logging, and tracing; ensuring services are measurable, debuggable, and aligned with reliability goals.\n\n - Evolving Incident Response Developing and improving incident response practices, from detection to post-incident learning, and helping teams build sustainable on-call and escalation patterns.\n\n - Enabling Self-Service Reliability Partnering with the platform team to build tooling and abstractions (e.g., service scorecards, dashboards, templates, golden paths) that make it easy for teams to adopt and stay compliant with reliability standards.\n\n - Driving Adoption Across Teams Working cross-functionally to educate, influence, and guide engineering teams—scaling reliability practices through a combination of clear standards, strong communication, and developer-friendly systems\n\nWho You Are\n\n - Experienced in production systems: You have 6+ years of experience operating and improving reliability of production systems at scale.\n\n - Strong foundation in cloud and infrastructure: You have hands-on experience with AWS, Kubernetes (e.g., EKS), and infrastructure as code tools like Terraform.\n\n - Deep understanding of reliability principles: You’ve defined or worked with SLOs/SLAs, understand error budgets, and have experience improving reliability through measurement and iteration.\n\n - Observability expertise: You’ve worked with modern observability tooling (we use DataDog) and understand how to build actionable monitoring systems across metrics, logs, and traces.\n\n - Systems thinker: You’re able to zoom out, identify patterns across teams and services, and design solutions that scale beyond a single system.\n\n - Impact-oriented: You focus on outcomes over output and care deeply about improving real reliability outcomes—not just adding processes.\n\n - Strong communicator and influencer: You can drive change across teams without direct authority, balancing pragmatism with long-term vision.\n\n - Self-directed: You thrive in ambiguous environments and are comfortable defining problems, proposing solutions, and executing independently.\n\n - Team player: You collaborate well, communicate with empathy, and enjoy mentoring and learning from others.\n\nBonus Points\n\n - You’ve helped introduce or scale reliability practices in a growing organization.\n\n - You’ve built internal tooling or platforms used by multiple teams.\n\n - You have experience designing service-level scorecards or compliance/reporting systems.\n\n - You’ve worked with both SaaS (e.g., DataDog) and self-managed observability stacks.\n\n - You were previously a product engineer and bring empathy for developer experience.\n\n - You have experience with database reliability and performance (we use PostgreSQL)\n\nWhy This Role Is Exciting\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to define what reliability looks like at a growing, scaling engineering organization—and to do it in a way that actually sticks.\n\nYou won’t just be responding to incidents or working within a single team. You’ll be shaping how reliability is measured, enforced, and experienced across the entire company. You’ll work alongside your team mates to turn best practices into intuitive, self-service systems that engineers rely on every day.\n\nYour work will directly improve system reliability, reduce incidents, and enable teams to move faster with confidence, ultimately making reliability a built-in property of how we build software at Grow.\n\n\n\n\nROLE DETAILS\n\n - Employment Type: Full Time, Exempt\n\n - Base Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $182,000–$250,000 USD Annually.\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our San Francisco, NYC, or Seattle hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$182K – $250K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$182K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"471b0b66-6b49-44c5-bc2b-93407a0dfb65","tierSummary":"$182,000–$250,000 USD Annually $182K – $250K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8ff4607e-d4bb-4a75-a375-602dc34db37f","summary":"$182,000–$250,000 USD Annually $182K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":250000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":250000}]}},{"id":"fa101721-1fba-42ae-a949-5389e82e11c0","title":"Senior/Staff  Security Engineer, Incident Response ","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}},{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T20:51:00.618+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/fa101721-1fba-42ae-a949-5389e82e11c0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/fa101721-1fba-42ae-a949-5389e82e11c0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2>The Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a Senior or Staff level role owning detection and incident response at Grow. The core of the job is: catching threats early through strong detection engineering, moving fast on unfamiliar systems when something does happen, and having a real point of view on where the architecture is exposed before it becomes a problem. It's cross functional by design, working closely with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You'll Be Doing</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share security judgment and standards with teams across the company, raising the bar beyond the security org itself</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate and resolve security incidents across endpoint, network, and cloud, understanding unfamiliar systems well enough to respond with confidence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research the threats and attack methods most relevant to a healthcare marketplace, and use that intelligence to get ahead of them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and mature Grow's detection and response program, and participate in an incident on call rotation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strengthen our cloud security posture in partnership with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build defense in depth through secure by default architecture and processes, thinking through the full lifecycle of a problem rather than just patching the immediate risk</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design new, creative approaches to catching threats early, not just tuning what already exists</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>You'll Be a Good Fit If</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 6+ years of experience in detection and incident response</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have real depth in AWS security: IAM, secure service configuration, CloudTrail, SCPs, AWS Organizations, Config, and the like</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have deep expertise responding to complex incidents and a strong grasp of detection engineering, including SIEM, EDR, and CSPM tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You care about how security work lands on the people around you, from customers whose data you protect to the engineers you partner with</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You write code to automate the tedious parts of the job, and you're comfortable with infrastructure as code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You collaborate well, both within a security team and across engineering more broadly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You think about the whole solution, not just the technology, and can weigh competing design choices with real conviction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You understand the current threat landscape and know how to assess risk against it</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> <strong> $217,000–$288,000 USD Annually </strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: $182,000- $240,000 USD Annually </strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role can be <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>) or <strong>fully remote.</strong> Both arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nThis is a Senior or Staff level role owning detection and incident response at Grow. The core of the job is: catching threats early through strong detection engineering, moving fast on unfamiliar systems when something does happen, and having a real point of view on where the architecture is exposed before it becomes a problem. It's cross functional by design, working closely with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Share security judgment and standards with teams across the company, raising the bar beyond the security org itself\n\n - Investigate and resolve security incidents across endpoint, network, and cloud, understanding unfamiliar systems well enough to respond with confidence\n\n - Research the threats and attack methods most relevant to a healthcare marketplace, and use that intelligence to get ahead of them\n\n - Build and mature Grow's detection and response program, and participate in an incident on call rotation\n\n - Strengthen our cloud security posture in partnership with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance\n\n - Build defense in depth through secure by default architecture and processes, thinking through the full lifecycle of a problem rather than just patching the immediate risk\n\n - Design new, creative approaches to catching threats early, not just tuning what already exists\n\n\n\n\nYOU'LL BE A GOOD FIT IF\n\n - You have 6+ years of experience in detection and incident response\n\n - You have real depth in AWS security: IAM, secure service configuration, CloudTrail, SCPs, AWS Organizations, Config, and the like\n\n - You have deep expertise responding to complex incidents and a strong grasp of detection engineering, including SIEM, EDR, and CSPM tooling\n\n - You care about how security work lands on the people around you, from customers whose data you protect to the engineers you partner with\n\n - You write code to automate the tedious parts of the job, and you're comfortable with infrastructure as code\n\n - You collaborate well, both within a security team and across engineering more broadly\n\n - You think about the whole solution, not just the technology, and can weigh competing design choices with real conviction\n\n - You understand the current threat landscape and know how to assess risk against it\n\n\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\n - Hybrid Commitment:  $217,000–$288,000 USD Annually \n\n - Fully Remote Commitment: $182,000- $240,000 USD Annually \n\nThis role can be hybrid (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday) or fully remote. Both arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $280K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $280K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"542a958e-9c27-4f82-941e-1f923621b4d3","tierSummary":"$220K – $280K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"31de895b-6543-4878-9847-566303d9f400","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"d195dea8-6d79-418e-a15f-2ef52687b8f5","summary":"$220K – $280K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":280000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":280000}]}},{"id":"76429bab-1895-4581-9785-4d3a3e670a02","title":"Staff Software Engineer - Developer Experience & Ai Enablement","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-31T14:46:47.115+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/76429bab-1895-4581-9785-4d3a3e670a02","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/76429bab-1895-4581-9785-4d3a3e670a02/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow Therapy's Developer Experience team exists to make our ~120 engineers (and growing) measurably faster and happier. We treat developer tools as a product: our customers are engineers, and everything we ship, from CI/CD and test infrastructure to build tooling and AI-native development workflows, is judged by whether it makes their day better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Staff Software Engineer to set technical direction for this work across the engineering organization. The team is small, fully senior, and largely greenfield: the goals are set at the org level and tracked by our most senior technology leaders, but the project list is yours to discover. Today, improvements to how teams build, test, and review code live in pockets. The staff engineer on this team turns pockets into paved roads: identifying the bottlenecks that cost every engineer time, designing the standard, and driving adoption across teams that do not report to you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on role on an AI-forward team. We are actively building agentic developer workflows and expect AI to be the primary lever in how we climb from AI-assisted to AI-native development.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the highest-leverage developer-experience problems across engineering end to end, deciding which bottleneck is worth solving, designing the approach, and driving org-wide adoption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and evolve engineering-wide standards for how teams build, test, and ship, and do the alignment work to make them stick as the org grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Making our large codebase fast to work in: build systems and monorepo tooling, CI/CD pipeline performance, test reliability and framework strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the golden paths for how engineers work with AI, find the highest-leverage places to push it deeper into the development loop, and keep Grow at the front of a fast-moving space.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive the technical strategy for breaking up the monolith, from the incremental migration path to the test-isolation and build tooling that makes it possible at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embedding with product teams to understand their workflows firsthand, and treating their feedback as product input</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raising the bar for the engineers around you through design review, mentorship, and the quality of your own shipped work</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have deep developer experience, developer productivity, or platform engineering experience where internal engineers were your customer, or you built developer tools as the product at a developer-tools company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have owned problems that only exist at scale: monorepo tooling, build systems (Bazel or similar), CI performance for large test suites, or test framework migrations, and you can speak to the before-and-after outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You think about developer tools with a product mindset, defining what success looks like up front and measuring adoption and developer satisfaction to know you've delivered it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You think about developer tools with a product mindset, measuring adoption and developer satisfaction rather than shipping and hoping</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are genuinely excited about AI development tooling and have opinions grounded in things you have built</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: Python ecosystem depth, GitHub Actions at scale, or prior experience driving standards across a 100+ engineer organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: you've built developer-facing AI tooling - coding agents, AI code review, LLM developer workflows, MCP - and have a grounded view of where it does and doesn't help.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt (or Non-Exempt)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$217,000–$289,000 USD Annually</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our San Francisco or Seattle hub locations <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nGrow Therapy's Developer Experience team exists to make our ~120 engineers (and growing) measurably faster and happier. We treat developer tools as a product: our customers are engineers, and everything we ship, from CI/CD and test infrastructure to build tooling and AI-native development workflows, is judged by whether it makes their day better.\n\nWe are looking for a Staff Software Engineer to set technical direction for this work across the engineering organization. The team is small, fully senior, and largely greenfield: the goals are set at the org level and tracked by our most senior technology leaders, but the project list is yours to discover. Today, improvements to how teams build, test, and review code live in pockets. The staff engineer on this team turns pockets into paved roads: identifying the bottlenecks that cost every engineer time, designing the standard, and driving adoption across teams that do not report to you.\n\nThis is a hands-on role on an AI-forward team. We are actively building agentic developer workflows and expect AI to be the primary lever in how we climb from AI-assisted to AI-native development.\n\n\n\nWhat You'll Be Doing:\n\n - Own the highest-leverage developer-experience problems across engineering end to end, deciding which bottleneck is worth solving, designing the approach, and driving org-wide adoption.\n\n - Set and evolve engineering-wide standards for how teams build, test, and ship, and do the alignment work to make them stick as the org grows.\n\n - Making our large codebase fast to work in: build systems and monorepo tooling, CI/CD pipeline performance, test reliability and framework strategy\n\n - Set the golden paths for how engineers work with AI, find the highest-leverage places to push it deeper into the development loop, and keep Grow at the front of a fast-moving space.\n\n - Drive the technical strategy for breaking up the monolith, from the incremental migration path to the test-isolation and build tooling that makes it possible at scale.\n\n - Embedding with product teams to understand their workflows firsthand, and treating their feedback as product input\n\n - Raising the bar for the engineers around you through design review, mentorship, and the quality of your own shipped work\n\n\n\nYou'll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have deep developer experience, developer productivity, or platform engineering experience where internal engineers were your customer, or you built developer tools as the product at a developer-tools company\n\n - You have owned problems that only exist at scale: monorepo tooling, build systems (Bazel or similar), CI performance for large test suites, or test framework migrations, and you can speak to the before-and-after outcomes\n\n - You think about developer tools with a product mindset, defining what success looks like up front and measuring adoption and developer satisfaction to know you've delivered it.\n\n - You think about developer tools with a product mindset, measuring adoption and developer satisfaction rather than shipping and hoping\n\n - You are genuinely excited about AI development tooling and have opinions grounded in things you have built\n\n - Bonus: Python ecosystem depth, GitHub Actions at scale, or prior experience driving standards across a 100+ engineer organization\n\n - Bonus: you've built developer-facing AI tooling - coding agents, AI code review, LLM developer workflows, MCP - and have a grounded view of where it does and doesn't help.\n\n \n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt (or Non-Exempt)\n\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $217,000–$289,000 USD Annually\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our San Francisco or Seattle hub locations three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.\n\n\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$217K – $289K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$217K - $289K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0516b9b2-ee05-4af7-8550-b16c80f20653","tierSummary":"$217K – $289K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"85f77a7c-2406-4b4b-92a6-5473c7bc032c","summary":"$217K – $289K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":217000,"maxValue":289000},{"id":"5db1dc51-e152-4568-a57e-8db567b6f485","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":217000,"maxValue":289000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"40326d35-cf61-4b93-bc39-2679c07b4332","title":"Senior/Staff Engineer, Cloud & Infrastructure Security","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}},{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T20:55:44.491+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/40326d35-cf61-4b93-bc39-2679c07b4332","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/40326d35-cf61-4b93-bc39-2679c07b4332/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2>The Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll build and mature our cloud security posture, working closely with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance to deliver secure products for the providers and patients on our platform. You'll also be in a rare position to shape how AI gets used in security here, not just adopting tools yourself, but designing agents that take on real security work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You'll Be Doing</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build the security foundation for Grow's infrastructure as it scales</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research the threats and attack methods most relevant to Grow's applications and infrastructure, and turn that research into real solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our cloud security posture in close partnership with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to security incidents, from critical to routine, and participate in an on call rotation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build defense in depth through secure by default architecture, closing gaps before they turn into incidents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and track the KPIs that show whether our cloud security program is actually working</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and deploy AI agents that strengthen threat detection, alert triage, vulnerability management, and incident response, reasoning through problems and escalating to a human when needed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2>You'll Be a Good Fit If</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in the Cloud Security domain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have deep AWS security experience: IAM, secure service configuration, CloudTrail, SCPs, AWS Organizations, Config, and similar tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have real depth in Kubernetes security, including secure deployments, network policies, service to service auth, RBAC, workload identity, admission controllers, and runtime security</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're comfortable with infrastructure as code  and think about the full lifecycle of a problem, not just the tool that patches it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You care about how your work lands on the people around you, from the patients whose data you protect to the teams you partner with, and you bring strong opinions to security design decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've actually built and deployed production grade AI agents or agent powered tools for security work, not just experimented with or advised on them</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> <strong>$182,000- $250,000 USD Annually </strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: $152,000–$208,000 USD Annually </strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role can be <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>) or <strong>fully remote.</strong> Both arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nYou'll build and mature our cloud security posture, working closely with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance to deliver secure products for the providers and patients on our platform. You'll also be in a rare position to shape how AI gets used in security here, not just adopting tools yourself, but designing agents that take on real security work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Design and build the security foundation for Grow's infrastructure as it scales\n\n - Research the threats and attack methods most relevant to Grow's applications and infrastructure, and turn that research into real solutions\n\n - Improve our cloud security posture in close partnership with infrastructure, engineering, and compliance\n\n - Respond to security incidents, from critical to routine, and participate in an on call rotation\n\n - Build defense in depth through secure by default architecture, closing gaps before they turn into incidents\n\n - Define and track the KPIs that show whether our cloud security program is actually working\n\n - Build and deploy AI agents that strengthen threat detection, alert triage, vulnerability management, and incident response, reasoning through problems and escalating to a human when needed\n\n\n\n\n\nYOU'LL BE A GOOD FIT IF\n\n - 6+ years of experience in the Cloud Security domain.\n\n - You have deep AWS security experience: IAM, secure service configuration, CloudTrail, SCPs, AWS Organizations, Config, and similar tooling\n\n - You have real depth in Kubernetes security, including secure deployments, network policies, service to service auth, RBAC, workload identity, admission controllers, and runtime security\n\n - You're comfortable with infrastructure as code  and think about the full lifecycle of a problem, not just the tool that patches it\n\n - You care about how your work lands on the people around you, from the patients whose data you protect to the teams you partner with, and you bring strong opinions to security design decisions\n\n - You've actually built and deployed production grade AI agents or agent powered tools for security work, not just experimented with or advised on them\n\n\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\n - Hybrid Commitment: $182,000- $250,000 USD Annually \n\n - Fully Remote Commitment: $152,000–$208,000 USD Annually \n\nThis role can be hybrid (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday) or fully remote. Both arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$152K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$152K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a97a7541-fcae-41aa-b981-95bdf0d64769","tierSummary":"$152K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"75748a4a-022f-48e5-9e0a-62073c7d4c3a","summary":"$152K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":152000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"0c078676-01ca-48ea-ac18-f20246eaa014","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":152000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"f52b2e2b-bc6e-4ece-a671-1d0ab2b13fcf","title":"Senior Planner","department":"Business","team":"Growth","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T23:29:16.065+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/f52b2e2b-bc6e-4ece-a671-1d0ab2b13fcf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/f52b2e2b-bc6e-4ece-a671-1d0ab2b13fcf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a <strong>Senior Planner </strong>to join the Brand Planning team and lead marketing strategy and execution for an emerging side of our growing business: Enterprise, Payor, and Partnerships. In this role, you’ll lead development of a marketing strategy for B2B audiences in close partnership with cross-functional leaders, including positioning and messaging, audience insights, channel planning, roadmaps and creative executions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll be the owner of insights and marketing initiatives related to these audiences, and act as the connective tissue between relevant product, creative, research, data, and other teams to ensure consistency and alignment to the overall company and brand strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is an experienced brand strategist or integrated marketer with a sharp POV, excellent ability to build trust across an organization, and translate ambiguity into actionable and clear plans. Agency and client side experience is a plus, deep B2B knowledge and experience is essential.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Architecting the B2B marketing approach,</strong> including understanding landscape, audiences, and most effective marketing channels and methods</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop B2B-specific positioning and messaging architectures</strong>, elevating unique insights into the enterprise, payor, and partnership industries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and own integrated campaign roadmaps</strong>, defining objectives and executional plans to bring campaigns to life effectively</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Serve as the liaison and connective tissue</strong> between the B2B business owners and the brand &amp; marketing team, ensuring effective partner support plus brand alignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner cross-functionally</strong> with creative, product, product marketing, lifecycle, research, data, and other relevant stakeholders to drive alignment and clarity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop insights and write creative briefs</strong> that translate complex business needs into inspiring direction for creative teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Facilitate campaign kickoffs, strategic working sessions, and creative reviews</strong>, ensuring all stakeholders are anchored to B2B strategy and campaign objectives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ensure all creative output ladders</strong> up to the broader brand strategy while addressing the distinct needs and expectations of B2B audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Implement scalable planning and communication rhythms</strong> that keep cross-functional partners aligned and work moving efficiently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evaluate campaign performance</strong> in partnership with analytics, using data to continuously refine messaging strategy and improve business impact</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in brand strategy, brand planning, or integrated marketing—with meaningful B2B experience, ideally spanning both agency and in-house environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong familiarity with B2B marketing dynamics, including longer sales cycles, hard to reach audiences, and specific seasonality dynamics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record of developing positioning and messaging for B2B audiences, multisided marketplace and/or health care experience a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated expertise in writing creative briefs, developing messaging frameworks, and translating complex business needs into clear strategic narratives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working cross-functionally in fast-moving organizations, with the instincts to build trust and drive alignment without direct authority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strategic yet hands-on approach—equally comfortable developing the vision and rolling up your sleeves to make it real</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication and influence skills, with the ability to navigate ambiguity and bring clarity to complex or emerging business areas</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, solutions-oriented mindset and a genuine passion for building brands with consistency and purpose</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt<br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> $161,000 - $197,000 USD Annually</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC hub location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>)<strong>.</strong> Arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWe’re looking for a Senior Planner to join the Brand Planning team and lead marketing strategy and execution for an emerging side of our growing business: Enterprise, Payor, and Partnerships. In this role, you’ll lead development of a marketing strategy for B2B audiences in close partnership with cross-functional leaders, including positioning and messaging, audience insights, channel planning, roadmaps and creative executions.\n\nYou’ll be the owner of insights and marketing initiatives related to these audiences, and act as the connective tissue between relevant product, creative, research, data, and other teams to ensure consistency and alignment to the overall company and brand strategy.\n\nThe ideal candidate is an experienced brand strategist or integrated marketer with a sharp POV, excellent ability to build trust across an organization, and translate ambiguity into actionable and clear plans. Agency and client side experience is a plus, deep B2B knowledge and experience is essential.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing\n\n - Architecting the B2B marketing approach, including understanding landscape, audiences, and most effective marketing channels and methods\n\n - Develop B2B-specific positioning and messaging architectures, elevating unique insights into the enterprise, payor, and partnership industries\n\n - Build and own integrated campaign roadmaps, defining objectives and executional plans to bring campaigns to life effectively\n\n - Serve as the liaison and connective tissue between the B2B business owners and the brand & marketing team, ensuring effective partner support plus brand alignment\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with creative, product, product marketing, lifecycle, research, data, and other relevant stakeholders to drive alignment and clarity\n\n - Develop insights and write creative briefs that translate complex business needs into inspiring direction for creative teams\n\n - Facilitate campaign kickoffs, strategic working sessions, and creative reviews, ensuring all stakeholders are anchored to B2B strategy and campaign objectives\n\n - Ensure all creative output ladders up to the broader brand strategy while addressing the distinct needs and expectations of B2B audiences\n\n - Implement scalable planning and communication rhythms that keep cross-functional partners aligned and work moving efficiently\n\n - Evaluate campaign performance in partnership with analytics, using data to continuously refine messaging strategy and improve business impact\n\nYou'll Be a Good Fit If You Have\n\n - 8+ years of experience in brand strategy, brand planning, or integrated marketing—with meaningful B2B experience, ideally spanning both agency and in-house environments\n\n - Strong familiarity with B2B marketing dynamics, including longer sales cycles, hard to reach audiences, and specific seasonality dynamics\n\n - A proven track record of developing positioning and messaging for B2B audiences, multisided marketplace and/or health care experience a plus\n\n - Demonstrated expertise in writing creative briefs, developing messaging frameworks, and translating complex business needs into clear strategic narratives\n\n - Experience working cross-functionally in fast-moving organizations, with the instincts to build trust and drive alignment without direct authority\n\n - A strategic yet hands-on approach—equally comfortable developing the vision and rolling up your sleeves to make it real\n\n - Exceptional communication and influence skills, with the ability to navigate ambiguity and bring clarity to complex or emerging business areas\n\n - A proactive, solutions-oriented mindset and a genuine passion for building brands with consistency and purpose\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\nHybrid Commitment: $161,000 - $197,000 USD Annually\n\nThis role is hybrid (onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday). Arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$161K – $197K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$161K - $197K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0063e554-fc98-4c39-bfdf-45f8447e99de","tierSummary":"$161K – $197K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a6524594-47e9-424a-9a0c-5947b8d06214","summary":"$161K – $197K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161000,"maxValue":197000},{"id":"f202d9dd-38e7-4139-8c61-39a29396f609","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161000,"maxValue":197000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"eb6b5a30-a02d-47b7-83ac-51839574d2d2","title":"Engineering Manager, Momentum","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-02T19:26:25.000+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/eb6b5a30-a02d-47b7-83ac-51839574d2d2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/eb6b5a30-a02d-47b7-83ac-51839574d2d2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Momentum team builds experiences that support our clients in their mental health journey outside of active care — the 167 hours a week they're not in a session. We're looking for an Engineering Manager to lead a full-stack, product-focused team through the next phase of that work: taking us from 0 to 1 as we learn what clients actually need, then from 1 to 100 as we build out the capabilities that serve those needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a build-from-the-ground-up role. You'll drive the early architecture decisions for a team that's still defining its shape, lead a mix of backend and mobile engineers, and partner closely with product and design to shape what we build. We're looking for someone excited about this product space who wants a real hand in defining Grow's inter-session strategy.<br /></p><h2><strong>Why This Role Matters</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Momentum is early. The team was recently formed and is establishing its footing, so the person in this seat has real influence over the team's technical foundation, its culture, and the direction of the product itself. You'll operate with meaningful ownership, move quickly, and see your work directly influence product direction, technical foundations, and patient support on a national scale.<br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead a full-stack team of backend and mobile engineers, hiring and growing them as the team scales from 0 to 1 to 100.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive early architecture decisions that will shape Momentum's technical foundation for years to come.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help define and influence Grow's inter-session strategy, working with product to figure out what clients need between sessions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use data and client insight to guide decisions, measure impact, and adjust course quickly as we learn.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop frameworks for execution, prioritization, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a team culture with strong operational rigor appropriate for a team that’s finding product-market fit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and coach a high-performance team that excels in execution, communication, and problem-solving.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent Momentum and its work to the broader engineering organization alongside peer EMs and leaders.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience as an engineering manager, plus 6+ years as an IC in backend or iOS engineering. Experience building systems used by mental health or healthcare professionals is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven backend or iOS engineering leadership with focus on high quality experiences and user centric mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product sense with the ability to articulate vision and drive it to execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to deliver complex programs in ambiguous environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly data-driven decision-making approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and cross-functional leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building high-performance teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founder's mindset: ownership, speed, scrappiness, problem-solving.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Established frameworks of force multiplication and leadership.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Role Details:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> $224,000–$300,000 USD Annually</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Arrangement:</strong> Hybrid, with required in-office presence 3 days per week at our San Francisco, New York, or Seattle office. This role also includes travel 2–3 times per year for company and department offsites.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThe Momentum team builds experiences that support our clients in their mental health journey outside of active care — the 167 hours a week they're not in a session. We're looking for an Engineering Manager to lead a full-stack, product-focused team through the next phase of that work: taking us from 0 to 1 as we learn what clients actually need, then from 1 to 100 as we build out the capabilities that serve those needs.\n\nThis is a build-from-the-ground-up role. You'll drive the early architecture decisions for a team that's still defining its shape, lead a mix of backend and mobile engineers, and partner closely with product and design to shape what we build. We're looking for someone excited about this product space who wants a real hand in defining Grow's inter-session strategy.\n\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS\n\nMomentum is early. The team was recently formed and is establishing its footing, so the person in this seat has real influence over the team's technical foundation, its culture, and the direction of the product itself. You'll operate with meaningful ownership, move quickly, and see your work directly influence product direction, technical foundations, and patient support on a national scale.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Lead a full-stack team of backend and mobile engineers, hiring and growing them as the team scales from 0 to 1 to 100.\n\n - Drive early architecture decisions that will shape Momentum's technical foundation for years to come.\n\n - Help define and influence Grow's inter-session strategy, working with product to figure out what clients need between sessions.\n\n - Use data and client insight to guide decisions, measure impact, and adjust course quickly as we learn.\n\n - Develop frameworks for execution, prioritization, and operational excellence.\n\n - Create a team culture with strong operational rigor appropriate for a team that’s finding product-market fit.\n\n - Build and coach a high-performance team that excels in execution, communication, and problem-solving.\n\n - Represent Momentum and its work to the broader engineering organization alongside peer EMs and leaders.\n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - 3+ years of experience as an engineering manager, plus 6+ years as an IC in backend or iOS engineering. Experience building systems used by mental health or healthcare professionals is a plus.\n\n - Proven backend or iOS engineering leadership with focus on high quality experiences and user centric mindset.\n\n - Strong product sense with the ability to articulate vision and drive it to execution.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to deliver complex programs in ambiguous environments.\n\n - Highly data-driven decision-making approach.\n\n - Excellent communication and cross-functional leadership.\n\n - Experience building high-performance teams.\n\n - Founder's mindset: ownership, speed, scrappiness, problem-solving.\n\n - Established frameworks of force multiplication and leadership.\n\n\n\n\nROLE DETAILS:\n\n - Employment Type: Full Time, Exempt\n\n - Base Compensation: $224,000–$300,000 USD Annually\n\nWork Arrangement: Hybrid, with required in-office presence 3 days per week at our San Francisco, New York, or Seattle office. This role also includes travel 2–3 times per year for company and department offsites.\n\n\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$225K – $300K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$225K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"39fa0167-f6af-4bfc-85ee-346bb7ba5f8d","tierSummary":"$225K – $300K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a62b3d44-f64d-4cbb-879d-b851ed457c82","summary":"$225K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":225000,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"284beaa8-5926-452c-ab55-1af544f85134","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":225000,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"4a729c5c-4781-4e99-b9be-e72131a30643","title":"Senior Business Data Analyst, Business Analytics","department":"Business","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T00:14:29.646+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/4a729c5c-4781-4e99-b9be-e72131a30643","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/4a729c5c-4781-4e99-b9be-e72131a30643/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a <strong>Senior Business Data Analyst, Business Analytics </strong>to play a critical role in enabling data-driven decision-making across the organization. You will partner with business leaders to scope, design, and build the appropriate analytical tools and metrics to answer strategic and operational questions. This will include defining and operationalizing key performance indicators (KPIs), uncovering insights through rigorous analysis, developing scalable dashboards and reporting frameworks, and ultimately translating data into business value. Success in this role is measured by the impact of insights on strategic and operational decisions, clarity of metrics delivered, and measurable improvements in business outcomes such as growth, efficiency, and customer satisfaction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Elicit and synthesize data-driven insights into clear narratives and recommendations that influence decision-making, including recurring business reviews, strategic planning sessions, and ad hoc deep dives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable business leaders to make data-driven decisions by translating their business needs into the appropriate analytical tools and metrics to answer strategic and operational questions such as identifying growth levers, diagnosing performance gaps, or evaluating initiative impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scope, design, build, and maintain dashboards, reporting tools, and data models to enable self-service access to key metrics and ensure data accuracy, consistency, and accessibility across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI tools to accelerate your workflow and increase the quality of your output via querying, modeling, and synthesizing findings. You validate AI-assisted work rather than taking it at face value, and you build with scalability in mind so your solutions hold up as reliable, reusable processes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll be a good fit if you are:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A Problem Solver:</em> You have 3+ years of experience in BI or data analytics at a high-growth tech startup. You’re able to identify business challenges based on metrics and analyses, and you’re ready to recommend solutions to improve business processes. You balance analysis with decisive execution to avoid “analysis paralysis.”</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong bonus: Experience solving data problems in a healthcare-related field (e.g., RCM, provider operations, value-based care, health tech SaaS).</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A data-driven decision maker:</em> You have expert-level SQL skills and are familiar with tools like Snowflake, DBT, Looker, Hex, and Retool. You spend most of your day building critical analyses and data visualizations to elicit data-driven insights. You use metrics and analyses to uncover insights, validate hypotheses, and guide operational decisions. You are able to dive deep to understand the full scope of data, including edge cases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>AI-native: </em>AI tools are part of how you naturally work day-to-day. You default to using AI to speed up querying, drafting, and synthesis, and you know when to lean on it versus when deeper manual analysis is warranted. You stay current on new tools and techniques and bring that thinking back to how the team works.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>An effective communicator</em>: You are adept at translating complex analytical concepts to non-technical stakeholders. You are comfortable presenting to executives, business leaders, engineers, PMs, and peers. You are expert at crafting compelling data stories through visualizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Mission-Driven:</em> You’re here to change the world, and you’re always connecting your work back to the importance of the Grow Therapy mission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Agile:</em> You thrive in a fast-paced, unpredictable environment, and you’re able to pivot as new priorities emerge. You are skilled at managing multiple stakeholders, projects, and timelines efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A Team Player:</em> You’re collaborative by nature, relish in camaraderie and group wins, and are looked to by your colleagues as a steadfast partner and source of encouragement.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt (or Non-Exempt)<br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$124,000–$139,000 USD Annually.<br /></strong>This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWe’re looking for a Senior Business Data Analyst, Business Analytics to play a critical role in enabling data-driven decision-making across the organization. You will partner with business leaders to scope, design, and build the appropriate analytical tools and metrics to answer strategic and operational questions. This will include defining and operationalizing key performance indicators (KPIs), uncovering insights through rigorous analysis, developing scalable dashboards and reporting frameworks, and ultimately translating data into business value. Success in this role is measured by the impact of insights on strategic and operational decisions, clarity of metrics delivered, and measurable improvements in business outcomes such as growth, efficiency, and customer satisfaction.\n\nWhat you’ll be doing:\n\n - Elicit and synthesize data-driven insights into clear narratives and recommendations that influence decision-making, including recurring business reviews, strategic planning sessions, and ad hoc deep dives.\n\n - Enable business leaders to make data-driven decisions by translating their business needs into the appropriate analytical tools and metrics to answer strategic and operational questions such as identifying growth levers, diagnosing performance gaps, or evaluating initiative impact.\n\n - Scope, design, build, and maintain dashboards, reporting tools, and data models to enable self-service access to key metrics and ensure data accuracy, consistency, and accessibility across teams.\n\n - Use AI tools to accelerate your workflow and increase the quality of your output via querying, modeling, and synthesizing findings. You validate AI-assisted work rather than taking it at face value, and you build with scalability in mind so your solutions hold up as reliable, reusable processes.\n\nYou’ll be a good fit if you are:\n\n - A Problem Solver: You have 3+ years of experience in BI or data analytics at a high-growth tech startup. You’re able to identify business challenges based on metrics and analyses, and you’re ready to recommend solutions to improve business processes. You balance analysis with decisive execution to avoid “analysis paralysis.”\n   \n   - Strong bonus: Experience solving data problems in a healthcare-related field (e.g., RCM, provider operations, value-based care, health tech SaaS).\n\n - A data-driven decision maker: You have expert-level SQL skills and are familiar with tools like Snowflake, DBT, Looker, Hex, and Retool. You spend most of your day building critical analyses and data visualizations to elicit data-driven insights. You use metrics and analyses to uncover insights, validate hypotheses, and guide operational decisions. You are able to dive deep to understand the full scope of data, including edge cases.\n\n - AI-native: AI tools are part of how you naturally work day-to-day. You default to using AI to speed up querying, drafting, and synthesis, and you know when to lean on it versus when deeper manual analysis is warranted. You stay current on new tools and techniques and bring that thinking back to how the team works.\n\n - An effective communicator: You are adept at translating complex analytical concepts to non-technical stakeholders. You are comfortable presenting to executives, business leaders, engineers, PMs, and peers. You are expert at crafting compelling data stories through visualizations.\n\n - Mission-Driven: You’re here to change the world, and you’re always connecting your work back to the importance of the Grow Therapy mission.\n\n - Agile: You thrive in a fast-paced, unpredictable environment, and you’re able to pivot as new priorities emerge. You are skilled at managing multiple stakeholders, projects, and timelines efficiently.\n\n - A Team Player: You’re collaborative by nature, relish in camaraderie and group wins, and are looked to by your colleagues as a steadfast partner and source of encouragement.\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt (or Non-Exempt)\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $124,000–$139,000 USD Annually.\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$124K – $139K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$124K - $139K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e584e893-b746-4efc-9780-f120e08e124e","tierSummary":"$124K – $139K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8f35e739-0d2a-4cfb-8265-cae98ddf380f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"e1db5b73-ec6f-43e8-a55d-96d65aa1aa86","summary":"$124K – $139K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":139000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":124000,"maxValue":139000}]}},{"id":"31f85f93-5202-4c30-99f6-b9c95af46562","title":"Director, Revenue Cycle Management Operations","department":"Business","team":"Insurance Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T20:22:06.105+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/31f85f93-5202-4c30-99f6-b9c95af46562","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/31f85f93-5202-4c30-99f6-b9c95af46562/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow's RCM org is at an inflection point — scaling operational maturity, integrating AI-driven automation, and preparing for increasingly complex payor partnerships. This role builds the operational foundation that makes that evolution possible. It's right for you if you're energized by building systems that didn't exist before, leading managers and teams through transformation, and owning the operational levers that directly drive a company's financial performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end RCM operational performance across eligibility, claim submission, follow-up, denials, contracts, and authorizations, translating department strategy into execution across your team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assess and evolve team structure as the org scales including span of control, role design, and team growth. You'll inherit a strong team and be expected to make it structurally stronger.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operationalize AI and automation tools across RCM workflows — partnering with Grow's Operations AI Center of Excellence to ensure your teams adopt new capabilities effectively and that human and automated work is distributed intentionally as these tools mature.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and evolve rigorous KPI reporting and operational dashboards that give leadership clear visibility into RCM performance — including Uncollected %, denial rates, clean claim rates, and payor-level collection trends.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 8+ years of progressive experience in revenue cycle management, including 3+ years managing managers in a multi-function RCM operations environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've owned end-to-end RCM performance metrics and operations (denial rates, clean claim rate, days in A/R) and can point to specific operational improvements you drove.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've worked in a high-growth or rapid-scaling environment (ideally in health tech) where processes, systems, and team structures were being built or redesigned in real time, not just maintained.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're a builder, not just an operator. You've stood up new processes, reporting frameworks, or team structures during a period of growth or transformation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've managed RCM operations across diverse payor types where each payor introduces distinct billing rules, authorization requirements, and contractual structures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've operated where RCM and adjacent functions meet (credentialing, enrollment, provider operations, or finance) and understand how upstream quality drives downstream collections performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience operationalizing automation or AI tools within operational workflows — you don't need to build the technology, but you know how to adopt it, measure its impact, and reshape team processes around it.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: </strong>$158,000 - 193,000 USD Annually</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> $189,000 - $231,000 USD Annually </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role can be <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>) or <strong>fully remote.</strong> Both arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nGrow's RCM org is at an inflection point — scaling operational maturity, integrating AI-driven automation, and preparing for increasingly complex payor partnerships. This role builds the operational foundation that makes that evolution possible. It's right for you if you're energized by building systems that didn't exist before, leading managers and teams through transformation, and owning the operational levers that directly drive a company's financial performance.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Own end-to-end RCM operational performance across eligibility, claim submission, follow-up, denials, contracts, and authorizations, translating department strategy into execution across your team.\n\n - Assess and evolve team structure as the org scales including span of control, role design, and team growth. You'll inherit a strong team and be expected to make it structurally stronger.\n\n - Operationalize AI and automation tools across RCM workflows — partnering with Grow's Operations AI Center of Excellence to ensure your teams adopt new capabilities effectively and that human and automated work is distributed intentionally as these tools mature.\n\n - Maintain and evolve rigorous KPI reporting and operational dashboards that give leadership clear visibility into RCM performance — including Uncollected %, denial rates, clean claim rates, and payor-level collection trends.\n\n\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have 8+ years of progressive experience in revenue cycle management, including 3+ years managing managers in a multi-function RCM operations environment.\n\n - You've owned end-to-end RCM performance metrics and operations (denial rates, clean claim rate, days in A/R) and can point to specific operational improvements you drove.\n\n - You've worked in a high-growth or rapid-scaling environment (ideally in health tech) where processes, systems, and team structures were being built or redesigned in real time, not just maintained.\n\n - You're a builder, not just an operator. You've stood up new processes, reporting frameworks, or team structures during a period of growth or transformation.\n\n - You've managed RCM operations across diverse payor types where each payor introduces distinct billing rules, authorization requirements, and contractual structures.\n\n - You've operated where RCM and adjacent functions meet (credentialing, enrollment, provider operations, or finance) and understand how upstream quality drives downstream collections performance.\n\n - You have experience operationalizing automation or AI tools within operational workflows — you don't need to build the technology, but you know how to adopt it, measure its impact, and reshape team processes around it.\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\nFully Remote Commitment: $158,000 - 193,000 USD Annually\n\nHybrid Commitment: $189,000 - $231,000 USD Annually \n\nThis role can be hybrid (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday) or fully remote. Both arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$158K – $231K • Offers Equity • Multiple Ranges","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$158K - $231K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"9c873b58-239a-4494-952f-52de114d99ab","tierSummary":"Hybrid Commitment (SF, NYC, or Seattle office 3x/week) $189K – $231K • Offers Equity","title":"Hybrid","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6322a9f6-ecc3-4350-a6d1-6a734f904f5c","summary":"Hybrid Commitment (SF, NYC, or Seattle office 3x/week) $189K – $231K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":189000,"maxValue":231000},{"id":"7cd490c0-c17d-46f3-8f07-bab01a4a8b07","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]},{"id":"b15a2edf-f835-41e5-8653-9b2241ef130d","tierSummary":"Fully Remote Commitment $158K – $193K • Offers Equity","title":"Remote ","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3000b355-da85-4b47-bce2-0e4300e06f89","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"ec854f8a-a433-4638-ac35-d7617483f3fa","summary":"Fully Remote Commitment $158K – $193K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":158000,"maxValue":193000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"minValue":158000,"maxValue":231000,"currencyCode":"USD","interval":"1 YEAR","compensationType":"Salary"},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","minValue":null,"maxValue":null,"interval":"1 YEAR"}]}},{"id":"1fa2678d-c587-4ef0-9268-2d1266b8bfe7","title":"Director, Lifecycle & Retention","department":"Business","team":"Growth","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T20:53:43.523+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/1fa2678d-c587-4ef0-9268-2d1266b8bfe7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/1fa2678d-c587-4ef0-9268-2d1266b8bfe7/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Director of Lifecycle &amp; Retention to lead the delivery of an excellent customer experience across our multi-sided marketplace. In this role, you’ll own retention and lifecycle marketing - accountable for both strategy and execution. You will develop learning agendas, partner on advanced measurement approaches, and ensure that every initiative delivers clear, measurable impact and business growth through excellent experiences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with Product, Engineering, Customer service, Finance, and Creative to build strategies with alignment, accelerate performance outcomes, and bring the right message to the right customer at the right time. You will also oversee our lifecycle team and lead cross-functional initiatives that strengthen our approach to engagement, cohort health, and long-term retention.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a seasoned lifecycle and retention leader who is deeply customer obsessed, with strong analytical instincts and a bias for action, fluency across CRM and lifecycle tooling, and a track record of turning insights into scaled, measurable business growth. You are equally versed in how to design marketing programs and in how to influence product decisions through how deeply you learn about customer behavior. You bring structure to complexity and know how to guide teams toward rigor, clarity, and meaningful performance outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>What You Will Be Doing</strong></em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop the strategy and roadmap for retention &amp; lifecycle marketing across our customer journeys, spanning onboarding to long term loyalty loops.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and manage learning agendas and experiment frameworks that validate performance and inform prioritization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and own retention measurement and data in partnership with Data and Finance, including cohort analysis, LTV modeling, churn prediction, and attribution mapping</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own lifecycle channels and messaging systems (email, push, in-app, SMS, and emerging formats), ensuring the right participant is reached with the right message at the right moment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop a world-class lifecycle and retention org</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate deeply with product and engineering teams to inform the roadmap, improve signal quality, and build the tracking and infrastructure that lifecycle programs depend on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Creative, Data, and Finance teams to set shared objectives, align on learning agendas, and drive accountability against measurable business growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate customer-level and cohort-level insights to guide optimization, product decisions, and resource investment - and ultimately drive improved customer outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional reviews, planning cycles, and post-mortems to ensure the organization has clear visibility into results and is operating strategically</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable systems, documentation, and workflows that support transparency, efficiency, and improved results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current with lifecycle trends, measurement standards, and platform capabilities to identify new opportunities for engagement and efficiency</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in our New York, NY hub, where we require an in-office presence three days per week.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You Will Be a Good Fit If You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in lifecycle marketing, retention, or CRM, ideally within a consumer marketplace and/or a high-growth performance-driven organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record of building and scaling lifecycle programs across multiple audiences that drive measurable business outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated expertise with cohort analysis, LTV and churn modeling, experimentation, attribution frameworks, and lifecycle and CRM platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities and the ability to translate data into actionable insights and clear recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience informing product decisions and partnering closely with product and engineering teams to ship against a shared roadmap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine obsession with the customer and a habit of grounding every decision in participant behavior and needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strategic and operational mindset, with the ability to set long-term direction while executing near-term objectives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication, collaboration, and stakeholder management skills across technical and non-technical teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A steady, proactive, solutions-oriented approach when navigating ambiguity or competing priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A relentless focus on measurable impact and driving real, durable business growth</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> $189,000 - $231,000 USD Annually </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC hub location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>)<strong>.</strong> Arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe are looking for a Director of Lifecycle & Retention to lead the delivery of an excellent customer experience across our multi-sided marketplace. In this role, you’ll own retention and lifecycle marketing - accountable for both strategy and execution. You will develop learning agendas, partner on advanced measurement approaches, and ensure that every initiative delivers clear, measurable impact and business growth through excellent experiences.\n\nYou will work closely with Product, Engineering, Customer service, Finance, and Creative to build strategies with alignment, accelerate performance outcomes, and bring the right message to the right customer at the right time. You will also oversee our lifecycle team and lead cross-functional initiatives that strengthen our approach to engagement, cohort health, and long-term retention.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a seasoned lifecycle and retention leader who is deeply customer obsessed, with strong analytical instincts and a bias for action, fluency across CRM and lifecycle tooling, and a track record of turning insights into scaled, measurable business growth. You are equally versed in how to design marketing programs and in how to influence product decisions through how deeply you learn about customer behavior. You bring structure to complexity and know how to guide teams toward rigor, clarity, and meaningful performance outcomes.\n\nWhat You Will Be Doing\n\n - Develop the strategy and roadmap for retention & lifecycle marketing across our customer journeys, spanning onboarding to long term loyalty loops.\n\n - Create and manage learning agendas and experiment frameworks that validate performance and inform prioritization\n\n - Build and own retention measurement and data in partnership with Data and Finance, including cohort analysis, LTV modeling, churn prediction, and attribution mapping\n\n - Own lifecycle channels and messaging systems (email, push, in-app, SMS, and emerging formats), ensuring the right participant is reached with the right message at the right moment\n\n - Lead and develop a world-class lifecycle and retention org\n\n - Collaborate deeply with product and engineering teams to inform the roadmap, improve signal quality, and build the tracking and infrastructure that lifecycle programs depend on\n\n - Partner with Product, Creative, Data, and Finance teams to set shared objectives, align on learning agendas, and drive accountability against measurable business growth\n\n - Evaluate customer-level and cohort-level insights to guide optimization, product decisions, and resource investment - and ultimately drive improved customer outcomes\n\n - Lead cross-functional reviews, planning cycles, and post-mortems to ensure the organization has clear visibility into results and is operating strategically\n\n - Develop scalable systems, documentation, and workflows that support transparency, efficiency, and improved results\n\n - Stay current with lifecycle trends, measurement standards, and platform capabilities to identify new opportunities for engagement and efficiency\n\nThis role is based in our New York, NY hub, where we require an in-office presence three days per week.\n\nYou Will Be a Good Fit If You Have\n\n - 10+ years of experience in lifecycle marketing, retention, or CRM, ideally within a consumer marketplace and/or a high-growth performance-driven organization\n\n - A proven track record of building and scaling lifecycle programs across multiple audiences that drive measurable business outcomes\n\n - Demonstrated expertise with cohort analysis, LTV and churn modeling, experimentation, attribution frameworks, and lifecycle and CRM platforms\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities and the ability to translate data into actionable insights and clear recommendations\n\n - Experience informing product decisions and partnering closely with product and engineering teams to ship against a shared roadmap\n\n - A genuine obsession with the customer and a habit of grounding every decision in participant behavior and needs\n\n - A strategic and operational mindset, with the ability to set long-term direction while executing near-term objectives\n\n - Exceptional communication, collaboration, and stakeholder management skills across technical and non-technical teams\n\n - A steady, proactive, solutions-oriented approach when navigating ambiguity or competing priorities\n\n - A relentless focus on measurable impact and driving real, durable business growth\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\nHybrid Commitment: $189,000 - $231,000 USD Annually \n\nThis role is hybrid (onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday). Arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$189K – $231K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$189K - $231K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e77bf882-8522-4e0f-8723-5b1dd2a742cf","tierSummary":"Hybrid Commitment (NYC office 3x/week) $189K – $231K • Offers Equity","title":"Hybrid","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fdeba522-67fe-43b7-9017-228f189f125c","summary":"Hybrid Commitment (NYC office 3x/week) $189K – $231K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":189000,"maxValue":231000},{"id":"bd4e41fd-17bd-4f39-a53a-d89aed7d60db","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":189000,"maxValue":231000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d03c4b6c-b708-4a23-91af-5c91fa33ad9b","title":"Senior Product Manager, Employer Products","department":"Technology","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T12:27:35.062+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d03c4b6c-b708-4a23-91af-5c91fa33ad9b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d03c4b6c-b708-4a23-91af-5c91fa33ad9b/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Senior/Staff Product Manager to help us scale the Employer vertical of Grow Therapy's Lives Covered team, owning the product suite that drives our Employer GTM motion. You'll manage our portfolio of live Employer accounts while building the next generation of employer product experiences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end product strategy and delivery for Grow's employer products, building an experience that meets the needs of both employers and employees</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Design, Enterprise Sales, and Data to identify opportunities to improve the existing employee experience and define future product features that are compelling for employers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with VP of Enterprise, VP of Corp Dev and Finance to scale our Employer vertical</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Great Fit If You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of product management experience and 10+ years of relevant experience in Enterprise/B2B products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable leading product in ambiguous, fast-moving, cross-functional environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional stakeholder management skills, with the ability to align diverse teams around a shared roadmap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills, with comfort in data analysis and data-driven decision-making</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong prioritization instincts — balancing short-term wins with long-term investments and focusing on what drives the most impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptable — comfortable navigating ambiguity, learning quickly, and adjusting as new information emerges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communicator, comfortable representing Grow Therapy in conversations with Employers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe are looking for a Senior/Staff Product Manager to help us scale the Employer vertical of Grow Therapy's Lives Covered team, owning the product suite that drives our Employer GTM motion. You'll manage our portfolio of live Employer accounts while building the next generation of employer product experiences.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing\n\n - Own the end-to-end product strategy and delivery for Grow's employer products, building an experience that meets the needs of both employers and employees\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Design, Enterprise Sales, and Data to identify opportunities to improve the existing employee experience and define future product features that are compelling for employers.\n\n - Partner closely with VP of Enterprise, VP of Corp Dev and Finance to scale our Employer vertical\n\nYou’ll Be a Great Fit If You Have\n\n - 5+ years of product management experience and 10+ years of relevant experience in Enterprise/B2B products\n\n - Comfortable leading product in ambiguous, fast-moving, cross-functional environments\n\n - Strong cross-functional stakeholder management skills, with the ability to align diverse teams around a shared roadmap\n\n - Strong analytical skills, with comfort in data analysis and data-driven decision-making\n\n - Strong prioritization instincts — balancing short-term wins with long-term investments and focusing on what drives the most impact\n\n - Adaptable — comfortable navigating ambiguity, learning quickly, and adjusting as new information emerges\n\n - Excellent communicator, comfortable representing Grow Therapy in conversations with Employers\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$182K – $225K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$182K - $225K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"997e9fb8-ce37-4166-844f-0a81dcd96ea3","tierSummary":"$182K – $225K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b3cf4b59-8e61-4ab3-a544-00651add4956","summary":"$182K – $225K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":225000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":225000}]}},{"id":"e3de4709-bddf-434a-9107-afa59ba6225a","title":"Director, Search & Discoverability","department":"Business","team":"Growth","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T17:34:22.789+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/e3de4709-bddf-434a-9107-afa59ba6225a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/e3de4709-bddf-434a-9107-afa59ba6225a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Director of Search &amp; Discoverability to own the strategy and operations for this critical and evolving point in the customer decision journey.  In this role, you'll oversee search and discoverability end to end—accountable for both strategy and execution, across SEO &amp; AEO, and every input that drives them, including broader search surfaces like YouTube, Reddit and other forums, and emerging discovery channels. You will develop learning agendas, partner on advanced measurement approaches, and ensure that every initiative delivers clear, measurable impact and business growth through durable, compounding visibility - ultimately building a world-class program.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with Product, Engineering, Content, Data, and Growth to build strategies with alignment, accelerate performance outcomes, and make sure we show up when and where customers are searching for the category and brand. You will oversee agencies and lead cross-functional initiatives that strengthen our approach to organic growth, content quality, and long-term discoverability.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a seasoned search leader who is both deeply strategic and an excellent operator, with strong analytical instincts and a bias for action, fluency across the technical and editorial inputs that drive ranking and share of voice across answer surfaces, and a track record of taking insights and getting the buy-in needed to turn these into scaled, measurable business growth. You are equally versed in how to build a durable SEO/AEO engine and in how to win on newer discovery surfaces like YouTube and community platforms and have a proven track-record of successful execution of the initiatives you lead. You bring structure and clarity to a highly complex space and know how to guide teams toward delivering meaningful performance outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop the strategy and roadmap for search and discoverability across all surfaces, spanning SEO, AEO, YouTube, forums like Reddit, and emerging discovery channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the full set of inputs that drive organic performance—technical, content, architecture, structured data, brand, and more</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and manage learning agendas and experiment frameworks that validate performance and inform prioritization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and own search measurement and data in partnership with Data and Finance, including rankings, share of voice, traffic quality, conversion, and attribution mapping</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee agency partners and build the Search &amp; Discoverability org</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate deeply with product and engineering teams to inform the roadmap, improve site and signal quality, and build the tracking and infrastructure that search programs depend on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functionally to set shared objectives, align on learning agendas, and drive accountability against measurable business growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate query-level, surface-level, and content-level insights to guide optimization, product decisions, and resource investment—and ultimately drive improved customer outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional reviews, planning cycles, and post-mortems to ensure the organization has clear visibility into results and is operating strategically</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable systems, documentation, and workflows that support transparency, efficiency, and improved results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current with search trends, algorithm and answer-engine shifts, and platform capabilities to regularly innovate and identify new opportunities for reach and efficiency</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in search, SEO/AEO and organic growth, ideally within a consumer marketplace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record of building and scaling search programs across multiple surfaces that drive measurable business outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are highly innovative and have experience pushing boundaries and finding unique and custom ways to solve problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A relentless focus on measurable impact and driving real, rapid and sustainable business growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated expertise across the inputs that drive search and discoverability outcomes —technical SEO, content strategy, structured data, authority building, and answer-engine optimization—plus fluency with newer discovery surfaces like YouTube and community platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities and the ability to translate data into actionable insights and clear recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience informing product decisions and partnering closely with product and engineering teams to ship against a shared roadmap with measurable results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine obsession with the customer and a habit of grounding every decision in how and where people find answers and information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strategic and operational mindset, with the ability to set long-term direction while executing near-term objectives with excellence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication, collaboration, and stakeholder management skills across technical and non-technical teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A steady, proactive, solutions-oriented approach when navigating ambiguity or competing priorities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt<br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$189,000–$231,000 USD Annually <br /></strong>This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWe are looking for a Director of Search & Discoverability to own the strategy and operations for this critical and evolving point in the customer decision journey.  In this role, you'll oversee search and discoverability end to end—accountable for both strategy and execution, across SEO & AEO, and every input that drives them, including broader search surfaces like YouTube, Reddit and other forums, and emerging discovery channels. You will develop learning agendas, partner on advanced measurement approaches, and ensure that every initiative delivers clear, measurable impact and business growth through durable, compounding visibility - ultimately building a world-class program.\n\nYou will work closely with Product, Engineering, Content, Data, and Growth to build strategies with alignment, accelerate performance outcomes, and make sure we show up when and where customers are searching for the category and brand. You will oversee agencies and lead cross-functional initiatives that strengthen our approach to organic growth, content quality, and long-term discoverability.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a seasoned search leader who is both deeply strategic and an excellent operator, with strong analytical instincts and a bias for action, fluency across the technical and editorial inputs that drive ranking and share of voice across answer surfaces, and a track record of taking insights and getting the buy-in needed to turn these into scaled, measurable business growth. You are equally versed in how to build a durable SEO/AEO engine and in how to win on newer discovery surfaces like YouTube and community platforms and have a proven track-record of successful execution of the initiatives you lead. You bring structure and clarity to a highly complex space and know how to guide teams toward delivering meaningful performance outcomes.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n - Develop the strategy and roadmap for search and discoverability across all surfaces, spanning SEO, AEO, YouTube, forums like Reddit, and emerging discovery channels\n\n - Own the full set of inputs that drive organic performance—technical, content, architecture, structured data, brand, and more\n\n - Create and manage learning agendas and experiment frameworks that validate performance and inform prioritization\n\n - Build and own search measurement and data in partnership with Data and Finance, including rankings, share of voice, traffic quality, conversion, and attribution mapping\n\n - Oversee agency partners and build the Search & Discoverability org\n\n - Collaborate deeply with product and engineering teams to inform the roadmap, improve site and signal quality, and build the tracking and infrastructure that search programs depend on\n\n - Partner with cross-functionally to set shared objectives, align on learning agendas, and drive accountability against measurable business growth\n\n - Evaluate query-level, surface-level, and content-level insights to guide optimization, product decisions, and resource investment—and ultimately drive improved customer outcomes\n\n - Lead cross-functional reviews, planning cycles, and post-mortems to ensure the organization has clear visibility into results and is operating strategically\n\n - Develop scalable systems, documentation, and workflows that support transparency, efficiency, and improved results\n\n - Stay current with search trends, algorithm and answer-engine shifts, and platform capabilities to regularly innovate and identify new opportunities for reach and efficiency\n\nQualifications\n\n - 10+ years of experience in search, SEO/AEO and organic growth, ideally within a consumer marketplace\n\n - A proven track record of building and scaling search programs across multiple surfaces that drive measurable business outcomes\n\n - Are highly innovative and have experience pushing boundaries and finding unique and custom ways to solve problems\n\n - A relentless focus on measurable impact and driving real, rapid and sustainable business growth\n\n - Demonstrated expertise across the inputs that drive search and discoverability outcomes —technical SEO, content strategy, structured data, authority building, and answer-engine optimization—plus fluency with newer discovery surfaces like YouTube and community platforms\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities and the ability to translate data into actionable insights and clear recommendations\n\n - Experience informing product decisions and partnering closely with product and engineering teams to ship against a shared roadmap with measurable results\n\n - A genuine obsession with the customer and a habit of grounding every decision in how and where people find answers and information\n\n - A strategic and operational mindset, with the ability to set long-term direction while executing near-term objectives with excellence\n\n - Exceptional communication, collaboration, and stakeholder management skills across technical and non-technical teams\n\n - A steady, proactive, solutions-oriented approach when navigating ambiguity or competing priorities\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $189,000–$231,000 USD Annually \nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$189K – $231K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$189K - $231K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6408dc67-038f-466b-8627-4b2526e1b9da","tierSummary":"$189K – $231K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"31ec3a72-44aa-4e05-9deb-252a7f204384","summary":"$189K – $231K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":189000,"maxValue":231000},{"id":"9417fca7-8ee4-47b1-bda3-da981a0cebd4","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":189000,"maxValue":231000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a73d3d6a-4eed-4e57-851d-d04809534048","title":"Senior Growth Manager, Strategic Partnerships","department":"Business","team":"Growth","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T21:33:22.267+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/a73d3d6a-4eed-4e57-851d-d04809534048","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/a73d3d6a-4eed-4e57-851d-d04809534048/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Sr. Growth Manager, Strategic Partnerships to build and scale the conversion journey across our strategic partner categories—including employer / EAP, primary care (PCP), and other high-value partnership types. In this role, you'll own demand generation and qualified lead conversion end to end—accountable for both strategy and execution. You will manage paid channels, optimize the full conversion funnel, and find new growth channels that ensure we hit our scale and efficiency goals while also building strong brand recognition and favorability.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with Strategic Partnerships, Sales, Product, Data, Finance, and Creative to develop strategies, accelerate performance outcomes against those strategies, and ultimately build this program into one of our largest, most successful growth channels. You will also own the pipeline that fuels our partnership growth and lead cross-functional initiatives that strengthen our approach to lead quality, funnel health, and sustainable yet rapid growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a seasoned growth marketer who is scrappy yet strategic, with strong customer instincts and a bias for action, fluency across paid channels and funnel optimization, and a track record of 0→1 and 1→many. You are equally versed in how to run efficient paid programs at scale and in how to identify and build entirely new growth channels from the ground up.  You’re excellent at working with your Data partners to build the right architecture and enrichment levels that can scale and deliver actionable outputs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Will Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the roadmap for generating qualified leads across strategic partner categories, including employers, primary care physicians,, and other partnership types</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage paid channels end to end—planning, execution, budget pacing, and optimization against efficiency and volume targets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the conversion funnel across every stage, from first touch to qualified lead, and drive continuous improvement in conversion rates and experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify, test, and scale new growth channels to expand reach and improve efficiency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and manage learning agendas and experiment frameworks that validate performance and inform prioritization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and own growth measurement and data that ensure strategic goal-setting, in partnership with Data and Finance, including funnel analytics, CAC, lead quality, and attribution mapping</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate deeply with Partnerships and Sales to align on target audiences, prioritization, lead quality, and optimizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate channel-level and funnel-level insights to guide optimization, investment decisions, and resource allocation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable systems, documentation, and workflows that support transparency, efficiency, and improved results that all of Partnerships can leverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current with growth trends, channel shifts, and platform capabilities to identify new opportunities for scale and efficiency</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This role is based in our New York, NY hub, where we require an in-office presence three days per week.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You Will Be a Good Fit If You Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in growth marketing, demand gen, or performance marketing, ideally within a consumer marketplace.  Account-based experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven track record of building and scaling lead-generation funnels that drive measurable business outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated expertise managing paid channels and optimizing multi-stage conversion funnels against scale and efficiency goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience identifying and building new growth channels from the ground up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical capabilities and the ability to translate data into actionable insights and clear recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering closely with partnerships, sales, product, and data teams to ship against shared goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine obsession with the customer and a habit of grounding every decision in customer behavior and needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strategic and operational mindset, with the ability to set long-term direction while executing near-term objectives with excellence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication, collaboration, and stakeholder management skills across technical and non-technical teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A steady, proactive, solutions-oriented approach when navigating ambiguity or competing priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A relentless focus on measurable impact and driving real, measurable business growth</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$161,000–$197,000 USD Annually<br /></strong>This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nWe are looking for a Sr. Growth Manager, Strategic Partnerships to build and scale the conversion journey across our strategic partner categories—including employer / EAP, primary care (PCP), and other high-value partnership types. In this role, you'll own demand generation and qualified lead conversion end to end—accountable for both strategy and execution. You will manage paid channels, optimize the full conversion funnel, and find new growth channels that ensure we hit our scale and efficiency goals while also building strong brand recognition and favorability.\n\nYou will work closely with Strategic Partnerships, Sales, Product, Data, Finance, and Creative to develop strategies, accelerate performance outcomes against those strategies, and ultimately build this program into one of our largest, most successful growth channels. You will also own the pipeline that fuels our partnership growth and lead cross-functional initiatives that strengthen our approach to lead quality, funnel health, and sustainable yet rapid growth.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a seasoned growth marketer who is scrappy yet strategic, with strong customer instincts and a bias for action, fluency across paid channels and funnel optimization, and a track record of 0→1 and 1→many. You are equally versed in how to run efficient paid programs at scale and in how to identify and build entirely new growth channels from the ground up.  You’re excellent at working with your Data partners to build the right architecture and enrichment levels that can scale and deliver actionable outputs.\n\n\n\nWhat You Will Be Doing:\n\n - Build the roadmap for generating qualified leads across strategic partner categories, including employers, primary care physicians,, and other partnership types\n\n - Manage paid channels end to end—planning, execution, budget pacing, and optimization against efficiency and volume targets\n\n - Own the conversion funnel across every stage, from first touch to qualified lead, and drive continuous improvement in conversion rates and experience\n\n - Identify, test, and scale new growth channels to expand reach and improve efficiency\n\n - Create and manage learning agendas and experiment frameworks that validate performance and inform prioritization\n\n - Build and own growth measurement and data that ensure strategic goal-setting, in partnership with Data and Finance, including funnel analytics, CAC, lead quality, and attribution mapping\n\n - Collaborate deeply with Partnerships and Sales to align on target audiences, prioritization, lead quality, and optimizations\n\n - Evaluate channel-level and funnel-level insights to guide optimization, investment decisions, and resource allocation\n\n - Develop scalable systems, documentation, and workflows that support transparency, efficiency, and improved results that all of Partnerships can leverage\n\n - Stay current with growth trends, channel shifts, and platform capabilities to identify new opportunities for scale and efficiency\n\n\n\nThis role is based in our New York, NY hub, where we require an in-office presence three days per week.\n\n\n\nYou Will Be a Good Fit If You Have:\n\n - 7+ years of experience in growth marketing, demand gen, or performance marketing, ideally within a consumer marketplace.  Account-based experience is a plus\n\n - A proven track record of building and scaling lead-generation funnels that drive measurable business outcomes\n\n - Demonstrated expertise managing paid channels and optimizing multi-stage conversion funnels against scale and efficiency goals\n\n - Experience identifying and building new growth channels from the ground up\n\n - Strong analytical capabilities and the ability to translate data into actionable insights and clear recommendations\n\n - Experience partnering closely with partnerships, sales, product, and data teams to ship against shared goals\n\n - A genuine obsession with the customer and a habit of grounding every decision in customer behavior and needs\n\n - A strategic and operational mindset, with the ability to set long-term direction while executing near-term objectives with excellence\n\n - Exceptional communication, collaboration, and stakeholder management skills across technical and non-technical teams\n\n - A steady, proactive, solutions-oriented approach when navigating ambiguity or competing priorities\n\n - A relentless focus on measurable impact and driving real, measurable business growth\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $161,000–$197,000 USD Annually\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$161K – $197K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$161K - $197K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"22764d44-c4f1-4511-a3f7-945d76c1ed39","tierSummary":"$161K – $197K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1b9af637-4d7b-4dae-84e3-329314703f24","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"572c95a3-998c-40c1-baa0-424632d6951d","summary":"$161K – $197K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161000,"maxValue":197000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":161000,"maxValue":197000}]}},{"id":"2cf6b8af-4bc3-4faf-a41b-390a3ebeaa8d","title":"Manager, Strategic Planning","department":"Business","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T02:09:56.159+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/2cf6b8af-4bc3-4faf-a41b-390a3ebeaa8d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/2cf6b8af-4bc3-4faf-a41b-390a3ebeaa8d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Manager, Strategic Planning to join our Business Operations team and own the systems and rhythms that enable Grow to plan and operate effectively as we scale. This is not a generalist BizOps role; it is focused specifically on the infrastructure that allows our leaders and teams to make good decisions, stay aligned, and execute with clarity. You will design, build, and run these processes end to end, from the Biweekly Business Review and OKR planning cycles to executive meetings, offsites, Town Halls, and internal communications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and continuously improve Grow's core operating rhythms -- including the Biweekly Business Review, OKR planning cycles, executive meeting cadences, and Town Halls -- ensuring they run with consistency, quality, and increasing efficiency over time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and facilitate executive offsites end to end: structure, pre-work, logistics, facilitation support, and post-offsite documentation and follow-through.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage OKR planning cycles from kickoff to completion: build the framework, own the timeline, facilitate cross-functional working sessions, and maintain the system of record.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary operational counterpart to Chiefs of Staff across Grow's functions, coordinating on cross-functional planning processes and company-wide initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI tools to improve the efficiency and quality of operating processes -- from automating coordination workflows to streamlining how information flows across the organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll be a good fit if you are:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>An Operator with Ownership Depth: </em>You have 5 to 7 years of experience in business operations, strategic operations, or a chief of staff function, ideally at a high-growth tech or healthcare company. You have personally built and run recurring operating processes -- not just supported them -- and you can speak to every decision you made and why.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A Systems Thinker: </em>You do not just run processes -- you think about why they exist and whether they are working. You can diagnose operational breakdowns, propose fixes, and implement them with limited oversight. You have strong intuitions about how planning, communication, and decision-making infrastructure should work at a scaling company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A Strong Project Manager: </em>You can build a project plan, manage complex timelines, coordinate across senior stakeholders, and ensure execution without losing sight of the objectives. Details do not fall through the cracks on your watch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Comfortable with the Full Range of the Work: </em>This role combines strategic process design with hands-on execution, including scheduling, logistics, and note-taking for executive meetings. You see both as part of the same job and do not minimize for the execution side.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A Senior Communicator: </em>You are equally comfortable designing a facilitation agenda for an executive offsite and drafting a company-wide communication. You can influence without authority, manage up effectively, and hold senior stakeholders to process expectations without being deferential or avoidant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>AI-Forward: </em>You actively use AI tools to improve your own productivity and the quality of the processes you run -- from automating coordination workflows to accelerating how information is synthesized and distributed. You see AI as a force multiplier and bring that mindset to everything you build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Mission-Driven: </em>You're here to change the world, and you connect your work back to the importance of the Grow Therapy mission.<br /><br /><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$144,000–$168,000 USD Annually <br /></strong>This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWe're looking for a Manager, Strategic Planning to join our Business Operations team and own the systems and rhythms that enable Grow to plan and operate effectively as we scale. This is not a generalist BizOps role; it is focused specifically on the infrastructure that allows our leaders and teams to make good decisions, stay aligned, and execute with clarity. You will design, build, and run these processes end to end, from the Biweekly Business Review and OKR planning cycles to executive meetings, offsites, Town Halls, and internal communications.\n\nYou will:\n\n - Own and continuously improve Grow's core operating rhythms -- including the Biweekly Business Review, OKR planning cycles, executive meeting cadences, and Town Halls -- ensuring they run with consistency, quality, and increasing efficiency over time.\n\n - Design and facilitate executive offsites end to end: structure, pre-work, logistics, facilitation support, and post-offsite documentation and follow-through.\n\n - Manage OKR planning cycles from kickoff to completion: build the framework, own the timeline, facilitate cross-functional working sessions, and maintain the system of record.\n\n - Serve as the primary operational counterpart to Chiefs of Staff across Grow's functions, coordinating on cross-functional planning processes and company-wide initiatives.\n\n - Leverage AI tools to improve the efficiency and quality of operating processes -- from automating coordination workflows to streamlining how information flows across the organization.\n\nYou’ll be a good fit if you are:\n\n - An Operator with Ownership Depth: You have 5 to 7 years of experience in business operations, strategic operations, or a chief of staff function, ideally at a high-growth tech or healthcare company. You have personally built and run recurring operating processes -- not just supported them -- and you can speak to every decision you made and why.\n\n - A Systems Thinker: You do not just run processes -- you think about why they exist and whether they are working. You can diagnose operational breakdowns, propose fixes, and implement them with limited oversight. You have strong intuitions about how planning, communication, and decision-making infrastructure should work at a scaling company.\n\n - A Strong Project Manager: You can build a project plan, manage complex timelines, coordinate across senior stakeholders, and ensure execution without losing sight of the objectives. Details do not fall through the cracks on your watch.\n\n - Comfortable with the Full Range of the Work: This role combines strategic process design with hands-on execution, including scheduling, logistics, and note-taking for executive meetings. You see both as part of the same job and do not minimize for the execution side.\n\n - A Senior Communicator: You are equally comfortable designing a facilitation agenda for an executive offsite and drafting a company-wide communication. You can influence without authority, manage up effectively, and hold senior stakeholders to process expectations without being deferential or avoidant.\n\n - AI-Forward: You actively use AI tools to improve your own productivity and the quality of the processes you run -- from automating coordination workflows to accelerating how information is synthesized and distributed. You see AI as a force multiplier and bring that mindset to everything you build.\n\n - Mission-Driven: You're here to change the world, and you connect your work back to the importance of the Grow Therapy mission.\n   \n   Employment Type: Full Time, Exempt \n   Base Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $144,000–$168,000 USD Annually \n   This is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n   The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$144K – $168K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$144K - $168K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c14ef383-7e42-46ce-992a-546a553fb915","tierSummary":"$144K – $168K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b3b83619-b3fc-4bf9-b37b-b3552ec5c8ff","summary":"$144K – $168K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":144000,"maxValue":168000},{"id":"96cbe09f-1099-4973-9f1e-3660cfafd4db","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":144000,"maxValue":168000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"2af57de6-4d80-44a5-8695-06bbee41cfb2","title":"Senior Manager, Business Analytics","department":"Business","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T23:47:17.257+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/2af57de6-4d80-44a5-8695-06bbee41cfb2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/2af57de6-4d80-44a5-8695-06bbee41cfb2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Senior Manager, Business Analytics</strong> to lead the team that powers data-driven decision-making across Grow. You'll manage the Business Analytics team of 5+ analysts and report into the Senior Director, Business Operations. The scope is horizontal by design: your team partners with leaders across Customer Ops, RCM, Credentialing, Clinical, Strategic Partnerships, Provider Experience, and Finance, giving each function the insights, reporting infrastructure, and recommendations they need to operate effectively. You will define the Business Analytics strategy, build scalable infrastructure, and lead the team that ensures leaders have the insights and tools they need to operate effectively</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong>:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and lead the Business Analytics strategy for every operational function at Grow, managing a pod-based team that supports Grow horizontally across multiple departments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner directly with department leaders to turn ambiguous business questions into clear analysis, and clear analysis into decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the development of dashboards, reporting frameworks, and KPIs that give departments what they need to operate and make decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and scale a team of analysts, moving them from executing requests to owning the recommendations that drive business impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build an AI-native analytics team by staying constantly current on new AI tools and capabilities for data and applying them to make your team more effective and efficient</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate insights and recommendations clearly to senior stakeholders, partnering with leaders to influence strategy, execution, and tradeoffs through data</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If</strong>:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 8+ years of experience in a quantitative role within fast paced technology environments, including experience leading data analytics teams that support multiple departments across a company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've managed a team of 5+ analysts and have experience scaling a team's size and its bar for output at the same time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You operate horizontally by instinct: comfortable holding many stakeholders and domains at once rather than specializing in one</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a track record of coaching analysts from \"technically correct\" to \"here's what this means and what we should do\"</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're outcomes-obsessed, and can point to specific business changes your team drove, not just the projects it shipped</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have genuine, hands-on fluency with AI tools, with a real example of turning AI-driven work into a measurable change in team output</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've operated in a growth-stage environment, and are comfortable with ambiguity and shifting priorities rather than running a narrow function inside a large, stable org</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have strong stakeholder management and communication skills, and are comfortable partnering with and presenting to senior leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are fluent in SQL with the ability to both set technical direction and roll up your sleeves on complex analyses or modeling work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a proven track record of partnering with Operations, Finance, and GTM teams to influence strategy, execution, and tradeoffs through data and clear communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are motivated by improving access to mental health care and energized by owning ambiguous, high impact problems</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt<br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$205,000–$250,000 USD Annually. <br /></strong>This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWe're looking for a Senior Manager, Business Analytics to lead the team that powers data-driven decision-making across Grow. You'll manage the Business Analytics team of 5+ analysts and report into the Senior Director, Business Operations. The scope is horizontal by design: your team partners with leaders across Customer Ops, RCM, Credentialing, Clinical, Strategic Partnerships, Provider Experience, and Finance, giving each function the insights, reporting infrastructure, and recommendations they need to operate effectively. You will define the Business Analytics strategy, build scalable infrastructure, and lead the team that ensures leaders have the insights and tools they need to operate effectively\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Define and lead the Business Analytics strategy for every operational function at Grow, managing a pod-based team that supports Grow horizontally across multiple departments\n\n - Partner directly with department leaders to turn ambiguous business questions into clear analysis, and clear analysis into decisions\n\n - Own the development of dashboards, reporting frameworks, and KPIs that give departments what they need to operate and make decisions\n\n - Lead, coach, and scale a team of analysts, moving them from executing requests to owning the recommendations that drive business impact\n\n - Build an AI-native analytics team by staying constantly current on new AI tools and capabilities for data and applying them to make your team more effective and efficient\n\n - Communicate insights and recommendations clearly to senior stakeholders, partnering with leaders to influence strategy, execution, and tradeoffs through data\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have 8+ years of experience in a quantitative role within fast paced technology environments, including experience leading data analytics teams that support multiple departments across a company.\n\n - You've managed a team of 5+ analysts and have experience scaling a team's size and its bar for output at the same time\n\n - You operate horizontally by instinct: comfortable holding many stakeholders and domains at once rather than specializing in one\n\n - You have a track record of coaching analysts from \"technically correct\" to \"here's what this means and what we should do\"\n\n - You're outcomes-obsessed, and can point to specific business changes your team drove, not just the projects it shipped\n\n - You have genuine, hands-on fluency with AI tools, with a real example of turning AI-driven work into a measurable change in team output\n\n - You've operated in a growth-stage environment, and are comfortable with ambiguity and shifting priorities rather than running a narrow function inside a large, stable org\n\n - You have strong stakeholder management and communication skills, and are comfortable partnering with and presenting to senior leadership\n\n - You are fluent in SQL with the ability to both set technical direction and roll up your sleeves on complex analyses or modeling work\n\n - You have a proven track record of partnering with Operations, Finance, and GTM teams to influence strategy, execution, and tradeoffs through data and clear communication.\n\n - You are motivated by improving access to mental health care and energized by owning ambiguous, high impact problems\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $205,000–$250,000 USD Annually. \nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$205K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$205K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ddc33bd1-0b33-4589-b95f-22122eda8a65","tierSummary":"$205K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6f5f4876-b815-4ee8-a664-30757daf04b5","summary":"$205K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":205000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"a9842301-437c-4910-af58-4c7c6ea85e87","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":205000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"3b5eabca-f87b-4118-b82e-4f715cb11a46","title":"Senior Manager, Marketing Operations","department":"Business","team":"Growth","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T20:47:01.227+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/3b5eabca-f87b-4118-b82e-4f715cb11a46","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/3b5eabca-f87b-4118-b82e-4f715cb11a46/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Marketing Operations Senior Manager to help bring clarity, structure, and momentum to our growing marketing and creative team. In this role, you’ll be the operational backbone of our creative process—leading cross-functional coordination, optimizing workflows, and ensuring we deliver high-quality creative work on time and on budget.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll partner closely with brand planning, design, copy, growth, legal, finance and media, and external vendors to manage end-to-end creative production. The ideal candidate is a master planner with a calm, solutions-oriented mindset, deep familiarity with creative workflows, and a passion for bringing order to creative chaos. The opportunity here is to be the architect of the system – designing the ideal workflow and process – and then running it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the end-to-end planning, execution, and delivery of creative projects, including digital campaigns, social content, video, and print</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee resource management and capacity planning across the creative team, ensuring optimal utilization of internal and external talent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a primary point of coordination between creative, growth and media, and other cross-functional teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propose, implement, and document scalable workflow processes that drive efficiency and clarity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain detailed project timelines, deliverables, and budgets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify project risks and blockers early, and implement solutions to keep work on track</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead project kickoffs, creative reviews, and postmortems, ensuring clear communication and accountability throughout</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure all creative output aligns with project goals, brand standards, and stakeholder expectations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own vendor management and contracting</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in our New York, NY hub where we require an in-office presence three days per week.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in account management, creative operations, or project management—ideally in an agency or in-house creative environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record managing digital-first campaigns and deliverables, with bonus points for experience in video and print</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in project management and collaboration tools (e.g., Notion, Workfront, Asana, Smartsheet, Adobe Creative Cloud, Slack, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to tell clear stories through presentations, spreadsheets, and written word</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical mindset with the ability to track performance and refine systems over time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills—you know how to keep everyone aligned without slowing down the work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of agency-style workflows, timelines, and team dynamics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment with multiple stakeholders and shifting priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A calm, proactive, detail-obsessed approach to managing complexity and deadlines</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don’t meet every single requirement, but are still interested in the job, please apply. Nobody checks every box, and Grow believes the perfect candidate is more than just a resume.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is <strong>$155,000–$190,000 USD Annually<br /></strong>This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nWe’re looking for a Marketing Operations Senior Manager to help bring clarity, structure, and momentum to our growing marketing and creative team. In this role, you’ll be the operational backbone of our creative process—leading cross-functional coordination, optimizing workflows, and ensuring we deliver high-quality creative work on time and on budget.\n\nYou’ll partner closely with brand planning, design, copy, growth, legal, finance and media, and external vendors to manage end-to-end creative production. The ideal candidate is a master planner with a calm, solutions-oriented mindset, deep familiarity with creative workflows, and a passion for bringing order to creative chaos. The opportunity here is to be the architect of the system – designing the ideal workflow and process – and then running it.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Manage the end-to-end planning, execution, and delivery of creative projects, including digital campaigns, social content, video, and print\n\n - Oversee resource management and capacity planning across the creative team, ensuring optimal utilization of internal and external talent\n\n - Serve as a primary point of coordination between creative, growth and media, and other cross-functional teams\n\n - Propose, implement, and document scalable workflow processes that drive efficiency and clarity\n\n - Develop and maintain detailed project timelines, deliverables, and budgets\n\n - Identify project risks and blockers early, and implement solutions to keep work on track\n\n - Lead project kickoffs, creative reviews, and postmortems, ensuring clear communication and accountability throughout\n\n - Ensure all creative output aligns with project goals, brand standards, and stakeholder expectations\n\n - Own vendor management and contracting\n\nThis role is based in our New York, NY hub where we require an in-office presence three days per week.\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - 10+ years of experience in account management, creative operations, or project management—ideally in an agency or in-house creative environment\n\n - Proven track record managing digital-first campaigns and deliverables, with bonus points for experience in video and print\n\n - Proficiency in project management and collaboration tools (e.g., Notion, Workfront, Asana, Smartsheet, Adobe Creative Cloud, Slack, etc.)\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to tell clear stories through presentations, spreadsheets, and written word\n\n - Analytical mindset with the ability to track performance and refine systems over time\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills—you know how to keep everyone aligned without slowing down the work\n\n - Deep understanding of agency-style workflows, timelines, and team dynamics\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment with multiple stakeholders and shifting priorities\n\n - A calm, proactive, detail-obsessed approach to managing complexity and deadlines\n\nIf you don’t meet every single requirement, but are still interested in the job, please apply. Nobody checks every box, and Grow believes the perfect candidate is more than just a resume.\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $155,000–$190,000 USD Annually\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC, hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$155K – $190K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$155K - $190K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3627c668-12b1-4989-bae8-a5b69dc010e4","tierSummary":"$155K – $190K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d22ce947-ca82-44b5-bbcf-1dcd7c66f876","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"fdd019d9-db9a-4c12-a38d-27443ed765e2","summary":"$155K – $190K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":190000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":155000,"maxValue":190000}]}},{"id":"31ba52c6-1ea7-46c6-b7d5-f6ad1df2b4a5","title":"Director, Business Recruiting","department":"Business","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T23:02:40.922+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/31ba52c6-1ea7-46c6-b7d5-f6ad1df2b4a5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/31ba52c6-1ea7-46c6-b7d5-f6ad1df2b4a5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1 in 4 people need mental health care, and most can't get it. Grow is building the infrastructure to change that, and the teams you help build will directly shape how quickly and how well we can expand access to care. As Director of Business Recruiting, you will own recruiting across Operations, Growth, Partnerships, Marketing, Finance, Legal, People, and Provider and Clinical teams - leaders and teams that will influence how we serve providers, partner with payors, reach patients, and scale the business.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow has reached meaningful scale, but we're still early enough that individual talent decisions can materially change our trajectory. You'll lead Business Recruiters who own distinct parts of the company, set the strategy for the function, and partner directly with senior leaders on critical talent and organizational decisions - while staying close enough to the work to personally lead our most important searches. This is a chance to shape how a high-growth company builds its leadership and teams, develop the next generation of recruiting leaders, and help Grow expand access to mental healthcare at a much larger scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Business Recruiting strategy across Operations, Growth, Partnerships, Marketing, Finance, Legal, People, and Provider and Clinical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate business priorities into workforce plans, recruiting strategy, and capacity decisions, anticipating talent needs before they become open requisitions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop senior Business Recruiters, setting a high bar for recruiting craft, sourcing, judgment, execution, and business partnership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with senior leaders on talent strategy, org design, profiles, leveling, compensation, and hiring decisions, using data and market insight to shape outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the bar on sourcing and talent advisory through market mapping, targeted outbound, pipeline discipline, and a strong point of view.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personally lead select critical and high-impact searches from market definition through close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the Business Recruiting performance narrative, defining the metrics that matter, diagnosing issues early, and translating recruiting outcomes into business decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve key recruiting programs, including referrals, interviewer certification, internal mobility, Bar Raiser expansion, and AI-enabled workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the team and leadership bench needed to scale, developing senior recruiters into stronger functional owners and future leaders.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12+ years of recruiting experience, with significant experience supporting business or non-technical functions in a fast-moving company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven people leadership experience managing experienced recruiters, raising standards, developing talent, and addressing underperformance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading recruiters who independently own senior stakeholders, business units, or complex hiring portfolios.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep recruiting craft across search strategy, market mapping, sourcing, assessment, stakeholder management, and closing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of personally leading complex, high-impact, and senior-level searches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong data fluency and operating discipline, with the ability to diagnose performance and turn insights into action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive judgment and influence, including the ability to challenge senior leaders and shape talent strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience translating business priorities into workforce and recruiting strategies across competing needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a high-growth environment that requires both strategic leadership and hands-on execution.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or scaling recruiting programs beyond core delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using modern recruiting technology, including AI, to improve sourcing, decision-making, and team effectiveness.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In your first few months, you’ll take ownership of Business Recruiting, establish clear priorities, and develop a data-backed point of view on where we can raise the bar.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From there, you’ll strengthen workforce planning, sourcing, talent advisory, and the rigor we bring to our most critical searches.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over time, success means Business Recruiting is a trusted partner to the business, senior recruiters operate as strong functional owners, and Grow makes better talent decisions because of the team you lead.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation: </strong>The base compensation range for this position is $189,000–$231,000 USD annually. The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment: </strong>This is a <strong>hybrid</strong> <strong>role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our New York City Hub location<strong> three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong>, and<strong> travel 2–3 times per year</strong> for company and department offsites.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\n1 in 4 people need mental health care, and most can't get it. Grow is building the infrastructure to change that, and the teams you help build will directly shape how quickly and how well we can expand access to care. As Director of Business Recruiting, you will own recruiting across Operations, Growth, Partnerships, Marketing, Finance, Legal, People, and Provider and Clinical teams - leaders and teams that will influence how we serve providers, partner with payors, reach patients, and scale the business.\n\nGrow has reached meaningful scale, but we're still early enough that individual talent decisions can materially change our trajectory. You'll lead Business Recruiters who own distinct parts of the company, set the strategy for the function, and partner directly with senior leaders on critical talent and organizational decisions - while staying close enough to the work to personally lead our most important searches. This is a chance to shape how a high-growth company builds its leadership and teams, develop the next generation of recruiting leaders, and help Grow expand access to mental healthcare at a much larger scale.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own Business Recruiting strategy across Operations, Growth, Partnerships, Marketing, Finance, Legal, People, and Provider and Clinical teams.\n\n - Translate business priorities into workforce plans, recruiting strategy, and capacity decisions, anticipating talent needs before they become open requisitions.\n\n - Lead and develop senior Business Recruiters, setting a high bar for recruiting craft, sourcing, judgment, execution, and business partnership.\n\n - Partner with senior leaders on talent strategy, org design, profiles, leveling, compensation, and hiring decisions, using data and market insight to shape outcomes.\n\n - Raise the bar on sourcing and talent advisory through market mapping, targeted outbound, pipeline discipline, and a strong point of view.\n\n - Personally lead select critical and high-impact searches from market definition through close.\n\n - Own the Business Recruiting performance narrative, defining the metrics that matter, diagnosing issues early, and translating recruiting outcomes into business decisions.\n\n - Evolve key recruiting programs, including referrals, interviewer certification, internal mobility, Bar Raiser expansion, and AI-enabled workflows.\n\n - Build the team and leadership bench needed to scale, developing senior recruiters into stronger functional owners and future leaders.\n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - 12+ years of recruiting experience, with significant experience supporting business or non-technical functions in a fast-moving company.\n\n - Proven people leadership experience managing experienced recruiters, raising standards, developing talent, and addressing underperformance.\n\n - Experience leading recruiters who independently own senior stakeholders, business units, or complex hiring portfolios.\n\n - Deep recruiting craft across search strategy, market mapping, sourcing, assessment, stakeholder management, and closing.\n\n - A track record of personally leading complex, high-impact, and senior-level searches.\n\n - Strong data fluency and operating discipline, with the ability to diagnose performance and turn insights into action.\n\n - Strong executive judgment and influence, including the ability to challenge senior leaders and shape talent strategy.\n\n - Experience translating business priorities into workforce and recruiting strategies across competing needs.\n\n - Comfort operating in a high-growth environment that requires both strategic leadership and hands-on execution.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building or scaling recruiting programs beyond core delivery.\n\n - Experience using modern recruiting technology, including AI, to improve sourcing, decision-making, and team effectiveness.\n\n\nWHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE\n\nIn your first few months, you’ll take ownership of Business Recruiting, establish clear priorities, and develop a data-backed point of view on where we can raise the bar.\n\nFrom there, you’ll strengthen workforce planning, sourcing, talent advisory, and the rigor we bring to our most critical searches.\n\nOver time, success means Business Recruiting is a trusted partner to the business, senior recruiters operate as strong functional owners, and Grow makes better talent decisions because of the team you lead.\n\n\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt\n\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $189,000–$231,000 USD annually. The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.\n\nHybrid Commitment: This is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our New York City Hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday), and travel 2–3 times per year for company and department offsites.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$189K – $231K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$189K - $231K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f796a181-267e-4eaa-84f3-97df38f4d11a","tierSummary":"$189K – $231K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"00da52d5-33f6-43ea-81c1-745ef1733ed7","summary":"$189K – $231K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":189000,"maxValue":231000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":189000,"maxValue":231000}]}},{"id":"3f7e9951-151d-4a80-9eff-79bf5cb440e9","title":"Specialist I, Provider Billing Support","department":"Business","team":"Customer Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T20:25:24.602+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/3f7e9951-151d-4a80-9eff-79bf5cb440e9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/3f7e9951-151d-4a80-9eff-79bf5cb440e9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Billing Support Specialist at Grow Therapy you will be at the forefront of our mission to make high-quality mental healthcare accessible and affordable. We are always working to demystify complex systems so that our patients and therapists are empowered with greater knowledge and choice. You will serve as a passionate advocate for both our Clients and Therapists, ensuring they feel heard and supported throughout their journey with us. You will play a crucial role at Grow by troubleshooting and resolving technical issues, assisting and educating customers on our platform, and identifying opportunities for continued customer growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll…</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and resolve issues Clients and Therapists raise via Phone and Live Chat.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dig deep into problems in order to help identify root causes and work with our Product teams to improve the platform overall</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist and educate customers on the Grow Therapy platform, providing great customer service to our Clients and Therapists.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the customer's go-to resource and passionate advocate, ensuring both Clients and Therapists feel heard and supported throughout their journey with Grow Therapy.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have one year of experience with insurance across multiple commercial &amp; government payers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a strong knowledge of medical terminology, ICD-10/ CPT codes preferable in mental health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience working within Claim MD or Availty verifying benefits, reading EOB’s, and are able to comprehensively explain benefits to patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience working within various payer portals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are self-motivated, eager to learn, and are comfortable with ambiguity / asynchronous communication</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You love problem solving; you’re naturally curious, especially about health tech</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your work ethic is defined by kindness and empathy, prioritizing Customer Experience over everything else</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are successful working independently and remotely, and adapt well to changing priorities and customer needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are comfortable meeting quantitative metrics, including the number of conversations you work on per day</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You thrive working at a fast-paced startup, and you are excited about contributing to our startup’s growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus points if bilingual (Spanish preferably)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Hourly, Non-Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The hourly compensation rate for this position is:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: </strong>$24.03 per hour</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is <strong>fully remote.</strong> Both arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don’t meet every single requirement, but are still interested in the job, please apply. Nobody checks every box, and Grow believes the perfect candidate is more than just a resume. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: Please upload your resume in PDF format </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\nAs a Billing Support Specialist at Grow Therapy you will be at the forefront of our mission to make high-quality mental healthcare accessible and affordable. We are always working to demystify complex systems so that our patients and therapists are empowered with greater knowledge and choice. You will serve as a passionate advocate for both our Clients and Therapists, ensuring they feel heard and supported throughout their journey with us. You will play a crucial role at Grow by troubleshooting and resolving technical issues, assisting and educating customers on our platform, and identifying opportunities for continued customer growth.\n\nIn this role, you’ll…\n\n - Troubleshoot and resolve issues Clients and Therapists raise via Phone and Live Chat.\n\n - Dig deep into problems in order to help identify root causes and work with our Product teams to improve the platform overall\n\n - Assist and educate customers on the Grow Therapy platform, providing great customer service to our Clients and Therapists.\n\n - Serve as the customer's go-to resource and passionate advocate, ensuring both Clients and Therapists feel heard and supported throughout their journey with Grow Therapy.\n   \n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have one year of experience with insurance across multiple commercial & government payers.\n\n - You have a strong knowledge of medical terminology, ICD-10/ CPT codes preferable in mental health\n\n - You have experience working within Claim MD or Availty verifying benefits, reading EOB’s, and are able to comprehensively explain benefits to patients.\n\n - You have experience working within various payer portals.\n\n - You are self-motivated, eager to learn, and are comfortable with ambiguity / asynchronous communication\n\n - You love problem solving; you’re naturally curious, especially about health tech\n\n - Your work ethic is defined by kindness and empathy, prioritizing Customer Experience over everything else\n\n - You are successful working independently and remotely, and adapt well to changing priorities and customer needs\n\n - You are comfortable meeting quantitative metrics, including the number of conversations you work on per day\n\n - You thrive working at a fast-paced startup, and you are excited about contributing to our startup’s growth\n\n - Bonus points if bilingual (Spanish preferably)\n\nEmployment Type: Hourly, Non-Exempt \nBase Compensation: The hourly compensation rate for this position is:\n\nFully Remote Commitment: $24.03 per hour\n\nThis role is fully remote. Both arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nIf you don’t meet every single requirement, but are still interested in the job, please apply. Nobody checks every box, and Grow believes the perfect candidate is more than just a resume. \n\nNote: Please upload your resume in PDF format \n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$20.00 – $24.03 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"eb6382b5-a5d2-47a9-869c-67602d616505","tierSummary":"$20.00 – $24.03 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"5ecafb18-4df7-41d1-8015-b4fe5421215e","summary":"$20.00 – $24.03 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20,"maxValue":24.03}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20,"maxValue":24.03}]}},{"id":"8ba4a0b8-055b-4822-9a5b-f0c02bbc4a32","title":"Specialist I, Client Billing Support","department":"Business","team":"Customer Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T17:54:05.624+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/8ba4a0b8-055b-4822-9a5b-f0c02bbc4a32","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/8ba4a0b8-055b-4822-9a5b-f0c02bbc4a32/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Billing Support Specialist at Grow Therapy you will be at the forefront of our mission to make high-quality mental healthcare accessible and affordable. We are always working to demystify complex systems so that our patients and therapists are empowered with greater knowledge and choice. You will serve as a passionate advocate for both our Clients and Therapists, ensuring they feel heard and supported throughout their journey with us. You will play a crucial role at Grow by troubleshooting and resolving technical issues, assisting and educating customers on our platform, and identifying opportunities for continued customer growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll…</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and resolve issues Clients and Therapists raise via Phone and Live Chat.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dig deep into problems in order to help identify root causes and work with our Product teams to improve the platform overall</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist and educate customers on the Grow Therapy platform, providing great customer service to our Clients and Therapists.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the customer's go-to resource and passionate advocate, ensuring both Clients and Therapists feel heard and supported throughout their journey with Grow Therapy.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have one year of experience with insurance across multiple commercial &amp; government payers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a strong knowledge of medical terminology, ICD-10/ CPT codes preferable in mental health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience working within Claim MD or Availty verifying benefits, reading EOB’s, and are able to comprehensively explain benefits to patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience working within various payer portals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are self-motivated, eager to learn, and are comfortable with ambiguity / asynchronous communication</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You love problem solving; you’re naturally curious, especially about health tech</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your work ethic is defined by kindness and empathy, prioritizing Customer Experience over everything else</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are successful working independently and remotely, and adapt well to changing priorities and customer needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are comfortable meeting quantitative metrics, including the number of conversations you work on per day</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You thrive working at a fast-paced startup, and you are excited about contributing to our startup’s growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus points if bilingual (Spanish preferably)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Hourly, Non-Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The hourly compensation rate for this position is:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: </strong>$24.03 per hour</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is <strong>fully remote.</strong> Both arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>If you don’t meet every single requirement, but are still interested in the job, please apply. Nobody checks every box, and Grow believes the perfect candidate is more than just a resume. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: Please upload your resume in PDF format </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\nAs a Billing Support Specialist at Grow Therapy you will be at the forefront of our mission to make high-quality mental healthcare accessible and affordable. We are always working to demystify complex systems so that our patients and therapists are empowered with greater knowledge and choice. You will serve as a passionate advocate for both our Clients and Therapists, ensuring they feel heard and supported throughout their journey with us. You will play a crucial role at Grow by troubleshooting and resolving technical issues, assisting and educating customers on our platform, and identifying opportunities for continued customer growth.\n\nIn this role, you’ll…\n\n - Troubleshoot and resolve issues Clients and Therapists raise via Phone and Live Chat.\n\n - Dig deep into problems in order to help identify root causes and work with our Product teams to improve the platform overall\n\n - Assist and educate customers on the Grow Therapy platform, providing great customer service to our Clients and Therapists.\n\n - Serve as the customer's go-to resource and passionate advocate, ensuring both Clients and Therapists feel heard and supported throughout their journey with Grow Therapy.\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have one year of experience with insurance across multiple commercial & government payers.\n\n - You have a strong knowledge of medical terminology, ICD-10/ CPT codes preferable in mental health\n\n - You have experience working within Claim MD or Availty verifying benefits, reading EOB’s, and are able to comprehensively explain benefits to patients.\n\n - You have experience working within various payer portals.\n\n - You are self-motivated, eager to learn, and are comfortable with ambiguity / asynchronous communication\n\n - You love problem solving; you’re naturally curious, especially about health tech\n\n - Your work ethic is defined by kindness and empathy, prioritizing Customer Experience over everything else\n\n - You are successful working independently and remotely, and adapt well to changing priorities and customer needs\n\n - You are comfortable meeting quantitative metrics, including the number of conversations you work on per day\n\n - You thrive working at a fast-paced startup, and you are excited about contributing to our startup’s growth\n\n - Bonus points if bilingual (Spanish preferably)\n\nEmployment Type: Hourly, Non-Exempt \nBase Compensation: The hourly compensation rate for this position is:\n\nFully Remote Commitment: $24.03 per hour\n\nThis role is fully remote. Both arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nIf you don’t meet every single requirement, but are still interested in the job, please apply. Nobody checks every box, and Grow believes the perfect candidate is more than just a resume. \n\nNote: Please upload your resume in PDF format \n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$20.00 – $24.04 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"af42911e-7b2b-4714-bebf-417d0c7c116a","tierSummary":"$20.00 – $24.04 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"a905aacd-47c5-4b37-b173-212ee6d8bd18","summary":"$20.00 – $24.04 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20,"maxValue":24.04}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20,"maxValue":24.04}]}},{"id":"d8357999-d9dc-4450-8d57-962037a9498d","title":"Authorization Supervisor","department":"Business","team":"Insurance Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T17:18:03.549+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d8357999-d9dc-4450-8d57-962037a9498d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/d8357999-d9dc-4450-8d57-962037a9498d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an experienced Authorization Supervisor to build and own our authorization function. This is a workstream that has outgrown its original home inside Eligibility and is now one of the most complex, highest-risk parts of our Pre-Bill operation, covering our WellHive partnership with the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Employee Assistance Program (EAP) partners (Cigna, Octave, Optum), and Kaiser populations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own the authorization-denial pipeline at the trend level, manage the Authorization Specialist and our outsourced authorization-entry team, and serve as the primary relationship owner for authorization-specific issues with key payer and partner contacts. You'll report directly to the Pre-Bill Operations Manager and work closely with the Eligibility, Billing, and Coding supervisors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This function increasingly runs on data and workflow tooling rather than manual queue work, so this role is as much about building and maintaining automated processes as it is about managing a team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Be Doing:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Authorization function is one of the most complex and highest-risk parts of Grow's Pre-Bill operation. As Authorization Supervisor, you'll own it end-to-end: the denial pipeline, the team that processes authorizations, and the partner relationships that keep it running. This role leans more toward building than managing an existing queue, so you'll spend real time standing up workflows and automation, not just overseeing one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>In this role, you will...</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the authorization denial pipeline at the trend level, identifying root causes across payers and driving resolution rather than fixing claims one at a time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain automated workflows that reduce manual authorization work over time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and develop an authorization team, including staffing, quality audits, and productivity standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own key partner relationships for authorization-specific issues, including escalations and process improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent the authorization function in cross-functional conversations with payor partnerships on escalation and process improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Billing, Eligibility, and Coding to resolve cross-functional authorization issues and escalate systemic trends</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare the function for new frameworks and partnerships as Grow expands</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 3+ years of experience in authorization, utilization management, patient access, or medical billing, including at least 1 year in a people management role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're SQL-fluent or can ramp up quickly, and you're comfortable directing and verifying data-driven, automated workflows, even if you're not writing every query yourself</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have prior people management experience, ideally in authorization, utilization management, or patient access</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're analytically minded and can spot a denial trend across payers rather than treating each case in isolation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're comfortable owning external partner relationships and escalating issues professionally</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're process-driven and can build and enforce repeatable workflows for a high-volume, high-complexity function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're adaptable and can ramp into a fast-moving, partially built environment without a long runway</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus points if you have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior VA Community Care Network or other government payer authorization experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior Employee Assistance Program experience (Cigna, Octave, or similar)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or scaling an operational function from an ad hoc or manual state</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on SQL or workflow-automation experience, even self-taught</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Salaried, Exempt<br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: </strong>$74,880-$84,240 USD Annually</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is <strong>fully remote.</strong> This arrangement may include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nWe are looking for an experienced Authorization Supervisor to build and own our authorization function. This is a workstream that has outgrown its original home inside Eligibility and is now one of the most complex, highest-risk parts of our Pre-Bill operation, covering our WellHive partnership with the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Employee Assistance Program (EAP) partners (Cigna, Octave, Optum), and Kaiser populations.\n\nYou'll own the authorization-denial pipeline at the trend level, manage the Authorization Specialist and our outsourced authorization-entry team, and serve as the primary relationship owner for authorization-specific issues with key payer and partner contacts. You'll report directly to the Pre-Bill Operations Manager and work closely with the Eligibility, Billing, and Coding supervisors.\n\nThis function increasingly runs on data and workflow tooling rather than manual queue work, so this role is as much about building and maintaining automated processes as it is about managing a team.\n\n\n\nWhat You'll Be Doing:\n\nThe Authorization function is one of the most complex and highest-risk parts of Grow's Pre-Bill operation. As Authorization Supervisor, you'll own it end-to-end: the denial pipeline, the team that processes authorizations, and the partner relationships that keep it running. This role leans more toward building than managing an existing queue, so you'll spend real time standing up workflows and automation, not just overseeing one.\n\nIn this role, you will...\n\n - Own the authorization denial pipeline at the trend level, identifying root causes across payers and driving resolution rather than fixing claims one at a time\n\n - Build and maintain automated workflows that reduce manual authorization work over time\n\n - Manage and develop an authorization team, including staffing, quality audits, and productivity standards\n\n - Own key partner relationships for authorization-specific issues, including escalations and process improvements\n\n - Represent the authorization function in cross-functional conversations with payor partnerships on escalation and process improvement\n\n - Partner with Billing, Eligibility, and Coding to resolve cross-functional authorization issues and escalate systemic trends\n\n - Prepare the function for new frameworks and partnerships as Grow expands\n\nYou'll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have 3+ years of experience in authorization, utilization management, patient access, or medical billing, including at least 1 year in a people management role\n\n - You're SQL-fluent or can ramp up quickly, and you're comfortable directing and verifying data-driven, automated workflows, even if you're not writing every query yourself\n\n - You have prior people management experience, ideally in authorization, utilization management, or patient access\n\n - You're analytically minded and can spot a denial trend across payers rather than treating each case in isolation\n\n - You're comfortable owning external partner relationships and escalating issues professionally\n\n - You're process-driven and can build and enforce repeatable workflows for a high-volume, high-complexity function\n\n - You're adaptable and can ramp into a fast-moving, partially built environment without a long runway\n\nBonus points if you have:\n\n - Prior VA Community Care Network or other government payer authorization experience\n\n - Prior Employee Assistance Program experience (Cigna, Octave, or similar)\n\n - Experience building or scaling an operational function from an ad hoc or manual state\n\n - Hands-on SQL or workflow-automation experience, even self-taught\n\nEmployment Type: Salaried, Exempt\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\nFully Remote Commitment: $74,880-$84,240 USD Annually\n\nThis role is fully remote. This arrangement may include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$74,880 – $84,240","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$74,880 - $84,240","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1c62208c-cb61-4539-9513-cc28998e99e3","tierSummary":"$74,880 – $84,240","title":"Remote","additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"91ee8eba-5a07-43e3-b40e-dc5f6904a5da","summary":"$74,880 – $84,240","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":74880,"maxValue":84240}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":74880,"maxValue":84240}]}},{"id":"8bf3ea5d-87c3-452a-9561-46bd67eb6810","title":"Senior/Staff Engineer, Application & Product Security","department":"Technology","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Seattle","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"98107","addressRegion":"Washington","streetAddress":"1448 NW Market ST, Suite 500 (office 05-136)","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Seattle"}}},{"location":"New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}},{"location":"Waterloo","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}}},{"location":"San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T19:05:12.250+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/8bf3ea5d-87c3-452a-9561-46bd67eb6810","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/8bf3ea5d-87c3-452a-9561-46bd67eb6810/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><h2>The Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll make the secure path - the easy path for our engineering org of roughly 145 engineers, baking secure defaults, CI guardrails, and threat modeling into the SDLC so security ships with the product instead of blocking it, including for our fast growing AI and agent features.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You'll Be Doing</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion a secure by default culture, building defense in depth into our frameworks, architecture, and everyday processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop security requirements and work directly with teams to build them into new applications and services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manually dig into our source code to build a real, working understanding of our products, not just a surface level view from tooling output</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive the product security roadmap in collaboration with product, engineering, and the wider security team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner across product, engineering, DevOps, and services to ship secure software without slowing teams down</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design solutions that resolve and mitigate vulnerabilities and risk, and research the threats and attack methods most relevant to Grow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run security risk assessments, hands on penetration testing, and threat modeling, and turn those findings into secure coding education for engineers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>You'll Be a Good Fit If</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 6+ years of experience in application or product security</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You code well enough to automate tedious work and build frameworks or services that solve real security problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've been hands on with microservice architectures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You collaborate well, both within a security team and across the wider engineering org</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You prioritize based on real risk, not just raw vulnerability counts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've rolled up your sleeves and built a deep understanding of a codebase, rather than just talking about SAST, DAST, and SBOM tooling from the outside</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You work well with product managers and service teams, not just engineers, and you genuinely care about the product and how it actually functions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time, Exempt <br /><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid Commitment:</strong> <strong> $217,000–$288,000 USD Annually </strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote Commitment: $182,000- $240,000 USD Annually </strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role can be <strong>hybrid</strong> (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location <strong>three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday</strong>) or <strong>fully remote.</strong> Both arrangements include travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nYou'll make the secure path - the easy path for our engineering org of roughly 145 engineers, baking secure defaults, CI guardrails, and threat modeling into the SDLC so security ships with the product instead of blocking it, including for our fast growing AI and agent features.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Champion a secure by default culture, building defense in depth into our frameworks, architecture, and everyday processes\n\n - Develop security requirements and work directly with teams to build them into new applications and services\n\n - Manually dig into our source code to build a real, working understanding of our products, not just a surface level view from tooling output\n\n - Drive the product security roadmap in collaboration with product, engineering, and the wider security team\n\n - Partner across product, engineering, DevOps, and services to ship secure software without slowing teams down\n\n - Design solutions that resolve and mitigate vulnerabilities and risk, and research the threats and attack methods most relevant to Grow\n\n - Run security risk assessments, hands on penetration testing, and threat modeling, and turn those findings into secure coding education for engineers\n\n\n\n\nYOU'LL BE A GOOD FIT IF\n\n - You have 6+ years of experience in application or product security\n\n - You code well enough to automate tedious work and build frameworks or services that solve real security problems\n\n - You've been hands on with microservice architectures\n\n - You collaborate well, both within a security team and across the wider engineering org\n\n - You prioritize based on real risk, not just raw vulnerability counts\n\n - You've rolled up your sleeves and built a deep understanding of a codebase, rather than just talking about SAST, DAST, and SBOM tooling from the outside\n\n - You work well with product managers and service teams, not just engineers, and you genuinely care about the product and how it actually functions\n\n\n\n\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Exempt \nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is:\n\n - Hybrid Commitment:  $217,000–$288,000 USD Annually \n\n - Fully Remote Commitment: $182,000- $240,000 USD Annually \n\nThis role can be hybrid (onsite from our NYC, San Francisco, or Seattle hub location three days per week: Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday) or fully remote. Both arrangements include travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$182K – $288K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$182K - $288K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0852b890-bac4-489f-bb67-cc693ebb9529","tierSummary":"$182K – $288K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6bfb2ee7-0064-41a8-b8e2-e23686bfbf0b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"5fa9dd76-dbec-435a-9bda-56443c3ce3a0","summary":"$182K – $288K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":288000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":182000,"maxValue":288000}]}},{"id":"8d0be304-d798-4685-af39-592361468a64","title":"Senior Product Marketing Manager","department":"Business","team":"Growth","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T00:27:20.209+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/8d0be304-d798-4685-af39-592361468a64","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/8d0be304-d798-4685-af39-592361468a64/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Senior Product Marketing Manager to own the provider side of our product marketing practice at Grow Therapy. You'll sit at the intersection of Product and Marketing, partnering closely with Product Managers, Design, and Growth to shape how we bring provider-facing features to market and drive meaningful product adoption across our provider base. This is a high-ownership role on a small, collaborative PMM team reporting directly to the Staff PMM. Your work will directly shape how thousands of therapists experience and engage with the tools they rely on to run their practice. Your responsibilities will include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and execute go-to-market strategy for provider-facing product launches, including positioning, messaging, and supporting collateral</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain provider segmentation and persona frameworks to ensure our marketing reflects how providers actually think and work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product to translate feature releases into clear, compelling narratives that drive awareness and product adoption among providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own provider-facing marketing channels and lifecycle touchpoints, coordinating across email, in-product, and community to move providers from awareness to adoption</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor provider feedback, market trends, and competitive activity to surface insights that inform both marketing strategy and product direction<br /><br /><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 3+ years of product marketing experience, ideally at a startup or in a high-growth environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've owned GTM end-to-end, from positioning and messaging to launch execution and channel strategy, and can point to how your work drove product adoption</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have hands-on experience owning email and in-product marketing channels, and are comfortable running experiments, reading performance data, and iterating based on what you learn</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're a strong cross-functional partner who leads with curiosity about users, seeks out feedback, and uses what you learn to sharpen messaging and strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare or marketplace experience is a plus, not a requirement<br /><br /><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full Time<br /><strong><br /></strong>This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong> with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location <strong>three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday)</strong> and travel <strong>2–3 times per year</strong> (e.g., company and department offsites).<br /><br /><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.</em></p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nWe're looking for a Senior Product Marketing Manager to own the provider side of our product marketing practice at Grow Therapy. You'll sit at the intersection of Product and Marketing, partnering closely with Product Managers, Design, and Growth to shape how we bring provider-facing features to market and drive meaningful product adoption across our provider base. This is a high-ownership role on a small, collaborative PMM team reporting directly to the Staff PMM. Your work will directly shape how thousands of therapists experience and engage with the tools they rely on to run their practice. Your responsibilities will include:\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Build and execute go-to-market strategy for provider-facing product launches, including positioning, messaging, and supporting collateral\n\n - Develop and maintain provider segmentation and persona frameworks to ensure our marketing reflects how providers actually think and work\n\n - Partner with Product to translate feature releases into clear, compelling narratives that drive awareness and product adoption among providers\n\n - Own provider-facing marketing channels and lifecycle touchpoints, coordinating across email, in-product, and community to move providers from awareness to adoption\n\n - Monitor provider feedback, market trends, and competitive activity to surface insights that inform both marketing strategy and product direction\n   \n   You’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n   \n   - You have 3+ years of product marketing experience, ideally at a startup or in a high-growth environment\n   \n   - You've owned GTM end-to-end, from positioning and messaging to launch execution and channel strategy, and can point to how your work drove product adoption\n   \n   - You have hands-on experience owning email and in-product marketing channels, and are comfortable running experiments, reading performance data, and iterating based on what you learn\n   \n   - You're a strong cross-functional partner who leads with curiosity about users, seeks out feedback, and uses what you learn to sharpen messaging and strategy\n   \n   - Healthcare or marketplace experience is a plus, not a requirement\n     \n     Employment Type: Full Time\n     \n     This is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n     \n     The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate’s working location.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$142.5K – $152K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$142.5K - $152K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"df51f580-4a77-4a42-a3cf-bc0657374efa","tierSummary":"$142.5K – $152K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4ac49401-0023-43ee-a3a2-40080b83e550","summary":"$142.5K – $152K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":142500,"maxValue":152000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":142500,"maxValue":152000}]}},{"id":"91583005-45ec-49cd-84bf-2941b27bc129","title":"Recruiting Coordinator","department":"Business","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T19:21:51.553+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/91583005-45ec-49cd-84bf-2941b27bc129","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/91583005-45ec-49cd-84bf-2941b27bc129/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Recruiting Coordinator,</strong> you'll be a vital partner to both candidates and our internal teams, helping ensure a seamless, human-first hiring experience. You’ll serve as a primary point of contact for scheduling interviews and maintaining our applicant tracking system, while also supporting key initiatives across our Talent Operations function. Your focus will be on creating a high-touch, inclusive, and efficient hiring process that reflects Grow Therapy’s values.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll balance detail-oriented execution with warm, empathetic communication, ensuring candidates feel informed and cared for, and internal stakeholders are set up for success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary scheduling coordinator for candidate interviews, primarily for the Tech Team, ensuring logistics run smoothly across hiring teams, time zones, and interview formats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate onsite interviews and act as the point of contact for candidates when they visit the office, providing white glove service and support</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own communication with candidates throughout the interview lifecycle - providing timely updates, answering questions, and sharing resources that reflect our values and brand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with recruiters and interview teams to support organized and consistent interview processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain data integrity in our applicant tracking system (ATS), ensuring accurate and up-to-date information across candidate and job records.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain internal documentation including SOPs, training materials, and communication templates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support cross-functional Talent projects including our new Early Talent initiative, aimed at process improvement, helping with documentation, implementation, and team-wide accountability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously seek opportunities to enhance the candidate experience by identifying bottlenecks, offering process suggestions, and advocating for inclusive practices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Great Fit If</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 1+ years of experience in a recruiting coordinator or talent operations role, ideally in a fast-paced or high-growth technology environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re highly organized, detail-oriented, and thrive when juggling multiple tasks and timelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re experienced with scheduling interviews and managing workflows within an ATS [Ashby experience is a plus].</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve worked with candidate records and pipelines, and understand the importance of clean, accurate data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You bring excellent written and verbal communication skills, and enjoy interacting with people in a friendly and professional manner.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re proactive, collaborative, and energized by finding ways to make processes more effective.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment Type: Full Time, Non-Exempt</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $32.00 - $37.00 USD per Hour</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nAs a Recruiting Coordinator, you'll be a vital partner to both candidates and our internal teams, helping ensure a seamless, human-first hiring experience. You’ll serve as a primary point of contact for scheduling interviews and maintaining our applicant tracking system, while also supporting key initiatives across our Talent Operations function. Your focus will be on creating a high-touch, inclusive, and efficient hiring process that reflects Grow Therapy’s values.\n\nYou’ll balance detail-oriented execution with warm, empathetic communication, ensuring candidates feel informed and cared for, and internal stakeholders are set up for success.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing\n\n - Serve as the primary scheduling coordinator for candidate interviews, primarily for the Tech Team, ensuring logistics run smoothly across hiring teams, time zones, and interview formats.\n\n - Coordinate onsite interviews and act as the point of contact for candidates when they visit the office, providing white glove service and support\n\n - Own communication with candidates throughout the interview lifecycle - providing timely updates, answering questions, and sharing resources that reflect our values and brand.\n\n - Partner closely with recruiters and interview teams to support organized and consistent interview processes.\n\n - Maintain data integrity in our applicant tracking system (ATS), ensuring accurate and up-to-date information across candidate and job records.\n\n - Develop and maintain internal documentation including SOPs, training materials, and communication templates.\n\n - Support cross-functional Talent projects including our new Early Talent initiative, aimed at process improvement, helping with documentation, implementation, and team-wide accountability.\n\n - Continuously seek opportunities to enhance the candidate experience by identifying bottlenecks, offering process suggestions, and advocating for inclusive practices.\n\nYou’ll Be a Great Fit If\n\n - You have 1+ years of experience in a recruiting coordinator or talent operations role, ideally in a fast-paced or high-growth technology environment.\n\n - You’re highly organized, detail-oriented, and thrive when juggling multiple tasks and timelines.\n\n - You’re experienced with scheduling interviews and managing workflows within an ATS [Ashby experience is a plus].\n\n - You’ve worked with candidate records and pipelines, and understand the importance of clean, accurate data.\n\n - You bring excellent written and verbal communication skills, and enjoy interacting with people in a friendly and professional manner.\n\n - You’re proactive, collaborative, and energized by finding ways to make processes more effective.\n\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Non-Exempt\n\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $32.00 - $37.00 USD per Hour\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation to work onsite from our NYC hub location three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday) and travel 2–3 times per year (e.g., company and department offsites).\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.\n\n \n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$32 – $37 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"5a6b6d80-cf26-4b2b-a1bd-2f7a3c4ce4b5","tierSummary":"$32 – $37 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8ed40b27-b80b-4917-899a-0636287ca45c","summary":"$32 – $37 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":32,"maxValue":37}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":32,"maxValue":37}]}},{"id":"6985a871-9916-41dd-bc01-67edf2005e4e","title":"Senior Business Recruiter (Short Term Contract)","department":"Business","team":"People","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T15:46:20.148+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/6985a871-9916-41dd-bc01-67edf2005e4e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/6985a871-9916-41dd-bc01-67edf2005e4e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re seeking a seasoned Senior Business Recruiter (Contract) at Grow Therapy. You will own a high volume of requisitions and will partner closely with hiring managers to deeply understand team priorities, role requirements, and long-term business goals. In this role, you will primarily support hiring across Operations and Marketing. This is a short term contract role (3-4 months).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate will be passionate about Grow Therapy’s mission to expand access to mental healthcare, bringing that enthusiasm into every candidate interaction to help us attract and hire the most talented team in our space. This position can be fully remote, or based in San Francisco or New York with in-office days Tuesday through Thursday at whichever hub location you're near.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the full-cycle recruitment process from role kick-off to close, including managing pipelines in Greenhouse, strategic sourcing, and maintaining a strong flow of recruiter screens.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own roles across all levels, with a focus on from entry-level to mid-level, but with room to flex for more senior roles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner strategically with hiring managers and department leaders to gain a deep understanding of requirements, advise on interview panels, and inform hiring decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate success in fast-paced, scaling environments where proactive outreach, process efficiency, and metric-based performance are key.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and execute advanced sourcing strategies on platforms like LinkedIn, Ashby, Juicebox and other sourcing channels to engage top-tier passive talent.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use data and funnel analytics to drive decisions that improve recruiting efficiency, optimize pipelines, and influence hiring managers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver an exceptional candidate experience, ensuring timely and clear communication while effectively selling Grow Therapy’s mission and technical vision.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll Be a Good Fit If:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 8+ years of recruiting experience, with at least 5 years focused on corporate roles in high-growth, scaling organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a highly skilled sourcer who enjoys building outbound pipelines to attract top technical talent, including passive candidates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a strong understanding of recruiting best practices, including evaluating competencies and collaborating with leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience with recruiting tools like Greenhouse, Ashby, Gem, and LinkedIn Recruiter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You thrive in fast-paced, high-volume recruiting environments, balancing multiple requisitions while maintaining quality and efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are passionate about mental health and accessible therapy, and you can effectively communicate Grow Therapy’s mission to candidates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have excellent communication, interpersonal, and stakeholder management skills, with a track record of influencing hiring teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You live in or can easily commute to San Francisco or New York.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Role Details:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Contract, 1099</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contract Length:</strong> 3-4 months</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Base Compensation:</strong> The base compensation range for this position is $70-$75 USD per hour.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Note: This is a 1099 contract position, and as such, does not include benefits provided to full-time employees.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nThe Opportunity:\n\nWe’re seeking a seasoned Senior Business Recruiter (Contract) at Grow Therapy. You will own a high volume of requisitions and will partner closely with hiring managers to deeply understand team priorities, role requirements, and long-term business goals. In this role, you will primarily support hiring across Operations and Marketing. This is a short term contract role (3-4 months).\n\nThe ideal candidate will be passionate about Grow Therapy’s mission to expand access to mental healthcare, bringing that enthusiasm into every candidate interaction to help us attract and hire the most talented team in our space. This position can be fully remote, or based in San Francisco or New York with in-office days Tuesday through Thursday at whichever hub location you're near.\n\nWhat You’ll Be Doing:\n\n - Manage the full-cycle recruitment process from role kick-off to close, including managing pipelines in Greenhouse, strategic sourcing, and maintaining a strong flow of recruiter screens.\n\n - Own roles across all levels, with a focus on from entry-level to mid-level, but with room to flex for more senior roles\n\n - Partner strategically with hiring managers and department leaders to gain a deep understanding of requirements, advise on interview panels, and inform hiring decisions.\n\n - Demonstrate success in fast-paced, scaling environments where proactive outreach, process efficiency, and metric-based performance are key.\n\n - Build and execute advanced sourcing strategies on platforms like LinkedIn, Ashby, Juicebox and other sourcing channels to engage top-tier passive talent.\n\n - Use data and funnel analytics to drive decisions that improve recruiting efficiency, optimize pipelines, and influence hiring managers.\n\n - Deliver an exceptional candidate experience, ensuring timely and clear communication while effectively selling Grow Therapy’s mission and technical vision.\n\nYou’ll Be a Good Fit If:\n\n - You have 8+ years of recruiting experience, with at least 5 years focused on corporate roles in high-growth, scaling organizations.\n\n - You are a highly skilled sourcer who enjoys building outbound pipelines to attract top technical talent, including passive candidates.\n\n - You have a strong understanding of recruiting best practices, including evaluating competencies and collaborating with leaders.\n\n - You have experience with recruiting tools like Greenhouse, Ashby, Gem, and LinkedIn Recruiter.\n\n - You thrive in fast-paced, high-volume recruiting environments, balancing multiple requisitions while maintaining quality and efficiency.\n\n - You are passionate about mental health and accessible therapy, and you can effectively communicate Grow Therapy’s mission to candidates.\n\n - You have excellent communication, interpersonal, and stakeholder management skills, with a track record of influencing hiring teams.\n\n - You live in or can easily commute to San Francisco or New York.\n\nRole Details:\n\nEmployment Type: Contract, 1099\n\nContract Length: 3-4 months\n\nBase Compensation: The base compensation range for this position is $70-$75 USD per hour.\n\nThe base compensation for this role will vary depending on several factors, including relevant experience, qualifications, and the candidate's working location.\n\nNote: This is a 1099 contract position, and as such, does not include benefits provided to full-time employees.\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$70 – $75 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"06cbebc5-21bc-4f94-ace8-82f0d2bddad9","tierSummary":"$70 – $75 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"13196c5e-8fc6-4288-8f75-6c96fa958441","summary":"$70 – $75 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":70,"maxValue":75}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":70,"maxValue":75}]}},{"id":"c7a21320-91c3-4055-966d-b72908bcffba","title":"Staff Product Manager, Growth","department":"Technology","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10005","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"100 Broadway, 3rd Floor","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T20:52:15.920+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"94104","addressRegion":"California","streetAddress":"351 California Street, Suite 1300","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/c7a21320-91c3-4055-966d-b72908bcffba","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/grow-therapy/c7a21320-91c3-4055-966d-b72908bcffba/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow Therapy exists to make mental health therapy accessible for everyone. This role owns the moment that makes that real: the first booking. You’ll be accountable for new client intakes on the platform, which means you own both the number that drives the business and the number that represents someone finally getting the care they need. You’ll launch the 0 to 1 bets that reach people before they know they need us, remove the friction between “I need help” and a booked first session, and build the platform that turns what works into what scales.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll own</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Awareness:</strong> unlock new channels, partnerships, and integrations (wearables, DTC lab testing, other health and tech platforms) so Grow is present when people think about their health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Consideration:</strong> own SEO, AEO, and social so Grow shows up in the moment of need, whether someone is searching, asking an AI, or scrolling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Conversion:</strong> turn intent into action by removing friction and building confidence at every step on our website and app, guiding clients to a booked first appointment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Referrals:</strong> make it natural for clients to bring Grow to friends and loved ones who need help too</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Platform:</strong> build the MarTech foundations that equip marketers to test, learn, and optimize landing pages, emails, and campaigns at scale</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How you’ll work</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead</strong> by defining the strategy, aligning executive stakeholders and driving execution while raising the bar within the team and broader product organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Launch 0→1</strong> bets that unlock significant net-new ways to reach clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Optimize </strong>the funnel end-to-end by running a rigorous, experiment-driven practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner</strong> deeply with our Marketing team, and collaborate both with peer teams within the Client pillar and across the other two sides of our marketplace — Providers and Payers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full Time Employee Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health Benefits</strong>: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow for Grow:</strong> No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Wellness</strong>: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays &amp; Winter Break</strong>: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Parental Leave</strong>: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons</strong>: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Wellness &amp; Development Stipend</strong>: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commuter Benefits:</strong> Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Home Office &amp; Meals</strong>: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks:</strong> A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Research shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Grow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Use of AI Tools: </strong>We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; <strong>they do not make final hiring decisions.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report\"><em> <u>AI Bias Audit Report</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Interview Recording:</strong> We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates.</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq\"><em> <u>Learn more</u></em></a><em>. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or</em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg\"><em> <u>opt out in advance</u></em></a><em>. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI-Assisted Recruiter Screen:</strong> For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>State-specific notices:</strong> Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Questions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us:\n\nGrow was born to tackle a critical challenge: making mental health care more effective and accessible for everyone. Since launching in 2020, 15 million sessions have started on Grow, and we've barely scratched the surface. We do it through a three-sided marketplace that empowers providers, augments insurance payors, and serves patients. Every solution we build reveals ten more waiting to be delivered, and that's just what gets us going. We've backed that ambition with more than $328M in funding, including our Series D at a $3B valuation from Sequoia Capital, Transformation Capital, TCV, SignalFire, Menlo Ventures, Goldman Sachs Alternatives, and others.\n\nAt Grow, the work you do can literally change someone's life. Your work here doesn't stay on a screen; it impacts whether someone can find, afford, and access quality care. That ambition sets us apart, and offers you an endless runway to impact one of the world's most urgent issues. We don’t have passenger seats here. Everyone is driving something that matters.\n\nThis work deserves real commitment. So if you thrive on meeting problems head on, untangling serious complexity, and working at pace with the sharpest yet kindest people around, you've come to the right place.\n\nGrow Therapy exists to make mental health therapy accessible for everyone. This role owns the moment that makes that real: the first booking. You’ll be accountable for new client intakes on the platform, which means you own both the number that drives the business and the number that represents someone finally getting the care they need. You’ll launch the 0 to 1 bets that reach people before they know they need us, remove the friction between “I need help” and a booked first session, and build the platform that turns what works into what scales.\n\nWhat you’ll own\n\n - Awareness: unlock new channels, partnerships, and integrations (wearables, DTC lab testing, other health and tech platforms) so Grow is present when people think about their health\n\n - Consideration: own SEO, AEO, and social so Grow shows up in the moment of need, whether someone is searching, asking an AI, or scrolling\n\n - Conversion: turn intent into action by removing friction and building confidence at every step on our website and app, guiding clients to a booked first appointment\n\n - Referrals: make it natural for clients to bring Grow to friends and loved ones who need help too\n\n - Platform: build the MarTech foundations that equip marketers to test, learn, and optimize landing pages, emails, and campaigns at scale\n\nHow you’ll work\n\n - Lead by defining the strategy, aligning executive stakeholders and driving execution while raising the bar within the team and broader product organization\n\n - Launch 0→1 bets that unlock significant net-new ways to reach clients\n\n - Optimize the funnel end-to-end by running a rigorous, experiment-driven practice\n\n - Partner deeply with our Marketing team, and collaborate both with peer teams within the Client pillar and across the other two sides of our marketplace — Providers and Payers\n\n\n\nFull Time Employee Benefits:\n\n - Health Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, and disability coverage.\n\n - Grow for Grow: No cost access to therapy through the Grow platform (available to US employees)\n\n - Financial Wellness: Retirement savings programs and equity opportunities to help you invest in your future.\n\n - Flexible Time Off, Paid Holidays & Winter Break: Flexible time off, company paid holidays (which vary by country), and a full company wide Winter Break to rest and recharge\n\n - Parental Leave: Up to 18 weeks of paid parental leave to support you and your growing family and a new child stipend.\n\n - Mental Health Mornings/Afternoons: Dedicated weekly flexible time for self care, whether that's therapy, exercise, journaling, time with family, or simply taking a break.\n\n - Wellness & Development Stipend: Annual stipend to support your personal wellbeing and professional growth, from fitness and education to books and learning resources.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre tax commuter benefits to support teammates working from one of our hub locations.\n\n - Home Office & Meals: Support for your home workspace plus meal benefits, with offerings tailored to both remote and hub based employees.\n\n - Additional Perks: A variety of wellbeing benefits, including wellness memberships, virtual care, pet insurance discounts (where available), and global travel assistance.\n\n\nResearch shows that some groups hesitate to apply unless they meet every qualification. If you’re excited about this role but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply. At Grow, we value diverse experiences, transferable skills, and the unique strengths each person brings.\n\nGrow Therapy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\n\n\nUse of AI Tools: We use certain AI and automated tools to support recruitment. These tools help our team review applications, organize interviews, detect potential application integrity issues, and maintain interview records; they do not make final hiring decisions.\n\nApplication Review: Ashby's AI-Assisted Application Review helps review application materials against role-specific criteria and may flag potential fraud or integrity issues for recruiter review. All advancement decisions are made by our human recruiting team after independent review. See Ashby's AI Bias Audit Report https://trust.ashbyhq.com/item/ai-bias-audit-report.\n\nInterview Recording: We use BrightHire to record interviews, supporting note-taking and consistency across candidates. Learn more https://help.brighthire.ai/en/articles/4484370-brighthire-for-candidates-faq. Interviews are confidential; you may ask your interviewer to stop recording anytime, or opt out in advance https://app.brighthire.ai/candidate-opt-out/kcrUeiitS5Khw5AcWW_jLg. Choosing not to be recorded will not, by itself, affect your candidacy.\n\nAI-Assisted Recruiter Screen: For select roles, BrightHire's AI features may help structure initial recruiter screens and organize interview notes. All responses are reviewed by our recruiting team; no hiring decisions are made by AI alone.\n\nState-specific notices: Depending on your location, you may have additional rights. Illinois: If AI analyzes a video interview, we'll provide notice, explain how it works and what it evaluates, and obtain consent beforehand. New York City: Where required, we'll provide at least 10 business days’ notice before using an automated employment decision tool and explain how to request an alternative process. Maryland: We do not use facial recognition to create facial templates during interviews unless required notice and written consent are obtained.\n\nQuestions, accommodation requests, requests for an alternative selection process, objections to recording, or concerns about AI use? Contact talentops@growtherapy.com. We’re happy to help or offer an alternative way to participate.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $250K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"dca9d7f3-b7d9-4ee1-89e7-92858a18ee37","tierSummary":"$200K – $250K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e945e761-0833-4b00-9646-78292fef430b","summary":"$200K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}